P.transport["npc:anastasia-hartwell"] = {
  hash = "b4d21f",
  fullHash = "1efddd",
  text = "Anastasia Hartwell. In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Anastasia Hartwell trains Forsaken and Horde mages in the arcane arts. She guides spellcasters in their studies and directs magical research and field work across Lordaeron and beyond. In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Anastasia Hartwell teaches Forsaken and Horde mages to channel arcane energies. Though Lordaeron has fallen to ruin, former human practitioners such as Anastasia preserve their scholarly traditions in undeath. She demands discipline in the practice of magic. Careless incantations can consume the untrained. Anastasia sends promising students into the field as well as teaching them spells. At Balnir Farmstead in eastern Tirisfal Glades, mages gather snapdragons to learn how far the plague has spread. In the Apothecarium, they visit Algernon's alchemist shop to capture invisible creatures of pure magic behind a strange disturbance. Her assignments bring them face to face with magic's dangers, even within their own city. Anastasia's connections reach beyond Tirisfal. As Horde spellcasters grow more skilled, she coordinates with trainers in distant lands, including Deino in Orgrimmar. She also directs advanced students to solitary masters such as Tabetha in the swamplands of Dustwallow Marsh. Her guidance keeps Forsaken mages connected to the Horde's wider magical pursuits.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_anastasia-hartwell-67ebd9aa0b881d2cb261/1-0000.mp3", duration = 83.6440816, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:apothecary-johaan"] = {
  hash = "b9e863",
  fullHash = "b9e863",
  text = "Apothecary Johaan. In Brill, Apothecary Johaan works on a plague for the Forsaken. The Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas have set him to lethal experiments on local plants and animals. In Brill, Apothecary Johaan works openly for the newly formed Royal Apothecary Society. Like his colleagues across Lordaeron, he follows direct orders to create biological and alchemical weapons. The Forsaken hope these weapons will secure their fragile future against the living and the Scourge alike.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_apothecary-johaan-4908c3185db41ddf65e3/1-0000.mp3", duration = 30.1453061, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:apothecary-renferrel"] = {
  hash = "863d36",
  fullHash = "863d36",
  text = "Apothecary Renferrel. At the Sepulcher, Apothecary Renferrel studies Silverpine’s corrupted wildlife and undead threats. He advances Forsaken alchemy, and travelers bring him volatile reagents and help investigate Scourge remnants. At the Sepulcher, Renferrel leads field research for the Royal Apothecary Society in Silverpine Forest. The society’s grand laboratories and high leadership are in Undercity, while he works in the field. He gathers native biological specimens, refines potent concoctions, and studies the grim ecology along Lordaeron’s western border.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_apothecary-renferrel-3c65dd924701c0dafcd8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 33.2277551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:aramis-hammerhand"] = {
  hash = "0e57d9",
  fullHash = "b2f95e",
  text = "Aramis Hammerhand. In Deathknell's chapel, Aramis Hammerhand teaches the newly risen Forsaken to fight with the Holy Light. They can call on its power, but it burns their decayed flesh and demands fierce discipline. In Deathknell's chapel, Aramis Hammerhand guides Forsaken who still hold to their former faith. Before the Scourge swept across the north, many people of Lordaeron answered the Silver Hand's call. Aramis survived Lordaeron's fall, then rose into undeath. He kept the martial and spiritual teachings of his former life, and now guides others who will not surrender their devotion. For the Forsaken, channeling the Holy Light takes fierce will. Its power burns necrotic flesh and stirs long-dead nerves into excruciating pain. Aramis teaches new paladins that faith means enduring this torment. He asks them to face the physical and spiritual cost of wielding a force opposed to their undead nature.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_aramis-hammerhand-05251a5a993cb74bc0c6/1-0000.mp3", duration = 53.4987755, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:arugal"] = {
  hash = "b4d729",
  fullHash = "cddb1b",
  text = "Arugal. In Shadowfang Keep, Arugal commands the worgen he summoned against the Scourge. Madness and grief have made the former Dalaran wizard their self-proclaimed father, while his power threatens Silverpine Forest. Before Lordaeron fell, Arugal belonged to the Kirin Tor. Some peers, including Dalar Dawnweaver, called him a charlatan who leaned on enchanted trinkets to make up for weak spellcraft. When the Scourge swept across the north during the Third War, Arugal searched for a weapon that could halt the undead. He used research by the late Dalaran mage Ur to pierce the veil between realms and summon the worgen. The ravenous beasts tore through the Scourge, but no one could contain their ferocity. Soon their hunger turned against innocent mortals. The worgen slaughtered the Scourge, then turned on the wizards who summoned them. They besieged the ancestral seat of Baron Silverlaine, whose keep fell to their claws and fangs. Silverlaine and his retainers died in the massacre. Guilt shattered Arugal's mind, but he did not flee his creation. He adopted the beasts as his own offspring and renamed the fortress Shadowfang Keep. There he holds the ramparts, surrounded by ghostly victims and loyal hound-packs.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_arugal-ac3a73b7c4addc1c610e/1-0000.mp3", duration = 71.6016327, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:baine-bloodhoof"] = {
  hash = "f3766e",
  fullHash = "1369bd",
  text = "Baine Bloodhoof. In Bloodhoof Village, Baine Bloodhoof guards his people and Mulgore. Cairne leads from Thunder Bluff, while Baine directs the village’s defense against gnolls and outside threats. Baine Bloodhoof grew up traveling with his nomadic people as Cairne’s son. They settled in Mulgore’s grasslands, where centaur clans remained a threat. After the Third War, Khiragg’s warband captured Baine, and grief nearly kept Cairne from leading the new settlements. Rexxar freed Baine, restoring Cairne’s spirit. Then the tauren stood with Thrall’s Horde against the invading Kul Tirans and secured their foothold on the continent. Baine lives among his kin in Bloodhoof Village, not at the capital mesas. As Cairne grows older, Baine carries more responsibility for the people and represents the next generation of tauren leadership. He directs braves and visiting allies against Palemane gnolls troubling the borders. He also watches for outside influences that threaten Mulgore’s natural balance. Baine faces encroachers who give little thought to spiritual balance. In eastern Mulgore, the goblin Venture Company cuts into the sacred landscape. Dwarven prospectors from Bael Modan dig ancestral soil at the Bael'dun Digsite. Baine urges a firm but measured response: warn the miners and destroy their equipment instead of rushing into needless bloodshed. He says their violent digging hurts the spirits of the earth, but the miners refuse to listen.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_baine-bloodhoof-c3c9ccc5dea3212be843/1-0000.mp3", duration = 85.524898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:bethor-iceshard"] = {
  hash = "5c0281",
  fullHash = "5c0281",
  text = "Bethor Iceshard. In the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard directs the Magic Quarter's arcane and shadow practitioners. He holds authority in Sylvanas's realm, though old friendships still mark his past. From the Temple of the Damned in the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard directs arcane and shadow practitioners. His keen mind and icy resolve earn respect and fear. His political and magical authority reaches magistrates across Lordaeron. He sends Forsaken agents after valuable grimoires and arcane disturbances, and against rival powers that threaten the Undercity's rule.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_bethor-iceshard-e82914e1aab916630ba4/1-0000.mp3", duration = 32.9404082, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:brewmaster-drohn"] = {
  hash = "04d8ab",
  fullHash = "d6a3ab",
  text = "Brewmaster Drohn. Above Ratchet's docks, Brewmaster Drohn tends his brewing craft. The orc lives just uphill from the port, making potent drinks with methods tied to the wandering pandaren Chen Stormstout. Travelers who find discarded kegs across Kalimdor are sent to Drohn's porch. Brewmaster Drohn brews from his home on the hill above Ratchet's goblin docks. Rather than devote himself to combat, the orc has given his craft to brewing. He lives peacefully in the neutral haven established by Gazlowe's Steamwheedle cartel. While many orcs favor coarse grog or simple spirits, Drohn works with rare ingredients, carefully balanced flavors, and methods seldom practiced among his kin. Brewmaster Drohn learned brewing through a mentor who studied under Chen Stormstout, the pandaren wanderer who fought beside Rexxar and the Horde during the founding of Durotar. Chen also taught Drohn to make Trogg Ale. When travelers find Chen's discarded kegs in the wilds, Drohn is the only local authority who can identify their ingredients and recreate the wanderer's potent brews.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_brewmaster-drohn-16b851e5d13e266b6ac0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 61.675102, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:brine"] = {
  hash = "c7576d",
  fullHash = "f84299",
  text = "Brine. On Blackthorn Ridge, Brine guides shaman initiates toward the spirits of water. This orc shaman teaches them to commune with the tides and earn their Water Totem. Brine lives on a hill in northern Blackthorn Ridge, far from the Barrens' trading posts. Though dry savannas surround her, she has devoted her life to understanding water. Shaman across the Horde seek her wisdom after mastering earth and fire. She teaches that water calls for patience and perspective, qualities few understand as deeply as she does. In her youth, Brine marched with her orc companions across the Hillsbrad Foothills and fought against human settlements. During the campaign, she came to Tarren Mill and found a humble well fed by fresh spring water. The well stayed in her memory as a sign of life amid devastation. It strengthened a lesson she had learned as a child: even in the darkest sorrow, a small token of hope can still be found.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_brine-af95d999b2dc849a70bf/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.9020408, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:cairne-bloodhoof"] = {
  hash = "5800f5",
  fullHash = "5a5527",
  text = "Cairne Bloodhoof. In Thunder Bluff, Cairne Bloodhoof leads the united tauren tribes. The High Chieftain joined their fate to Thrall’s Horde after the orcs helped them escape extinction at centaur hands. Cairne Bloodhoof led the tauren from a life of flight to a home in Mulgore. For generations, centaur marauders hunted the tribes across the Barrens and drove them toward extinction. When Thrall and his orcs reached Kalimdor, Cairne saw a rare nobility in them.\n\nThrall offered protection and an escort for Cairne’s desperate caravan across the plains. In return, Cairne guided them to the Oracle at Stonetalon Peak. The tauren settled on Thunder Bluff’s towering mesas, where Cairne united the tribes and gave them a permanent home. Cairne Bloodhoof fought beside Thrall’s Horde and Jaina Proudmoore’s humans against the Burning Legion during the Third War. Grateful to Thrall, Cairne had followed the orcs to Stonetalon Peak. When Admiral Daelin Proudmoore invaded Durotar, Cairne took up arms again beside Rexxar. His captured son, Baine, had been safely recovered. Now one of the Horde’s most respected elders, Cairne remains Thrall’s closest confidant. He offers calm counsel against reckless warmongering.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_cairne-bloodhoof-3df0a690bcf6085f81b1/1-0000.mp3", duration = 73.5346939, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:canaga-earthcaller"] = {
  hash = "64c706",
  fullHash = "338fc8",
  text = "Canaga Earthcaller. In the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller guides new Horde shamans toward the spirits of the land and their first totems. Canaga Earthcaller guides Darkspear trolls and orcs who begin the shaman’s path from the red bluffs of the Valley of Trials. He teaches newcomers to quiet their minds and listen to Kalimdor’s rumblings. They prepare earth sapta so they can commune with the spirits. Canaga asks each novice to gather sacred reagents and travel to the local spirit rock in Durotar. There, they drink earth sapta and see the elemental spirits firsthand. Through his guidance, they earn their Earth Totem.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_canaga-earthcaller-9317318dc2b1fd1e814f/1-0000.mp3", duration = 36.1012245, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:carendin-halgar"] = {
  hash = "6ce565",
  fullHash = "6ce565",
  text = "Carendin Halgar. In the Undercity's Magic Quarter, Carendin Halgar teaches the Forsaken dark arts. His students learn to bind demons from the Twisting Nether, including Voidwalkers and Succubi. Carendin Halgar trains warlocks in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. He demands focus and obedience, and has little patience for failure, hesitation, or weakness. His students pass beyond simple incantations to summon demons and manipulate souls. Under his direction, they learn how the Forsaken make demons serve.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_carendin-halgar-c479c0869e60031f4266/1-0000.mp3", duration = 31.6865306, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:chief-hawkwind"] = {
  hash = "9d1df3",
  fullHash = "faa69c",
  text = "Chief Hawkwind. At Camp Narache, Chief Hawkwind readies young Shu'halo for life beyond Red Cloud Mesa. He guides their traditional rites in Mulgore and teaches humility, respect for the land, and the strength to protect their people. At Camp Narache, Chief Hawkwind prepares young tauren for life beyond Red Cloud Mesa. Fledgling hunters, shamans, druids, and warriors undertake the ancient Rites of the Earthmother on the mesa. Hawkwind oversees their customs and teaches each youth duty and endurance before they leave its safety. Chief Hawkwind begins with humility, not martial glory. He sends initiates to fetch clean spring water and perform simple chores, teaching reverence for nature and their elders. Once they show humility, the braves face tests of martial skill. Their trials test their resolve against aggressive Bristleback quilboar encroaching on the ancestral plains. Danger presses close to Camp Narache. The Bristleback tribe grows bolder along Red Cloud Mesa's perimeter. Hawkwind coordinates the settlement's defense and sends newly proven braves to blunt quilboar assaults and keep the sacred training grounds secure.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_chief-hawkwind-e5cf0ac9023eb61a0fa5/1-0000.mp3", duration = 68.9110204, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:coleman-farthing"] = {
  hash = "e6c443",
  fullHash = "2c39f1",
  text = "Coleman Farthing. At Brill's Gallows' End Tavern, Coleman Farthing still nurses a hatred born at the Agamand Mills. He served the wealthy Agamand dynasty in northern Tirisfal. He and the other laborers died defending their employers' estate from the Scourge. Now Forsaken, Coleman seeks vengeance on his former masters. Before the Third War, Coleman Farthing worked at the Agamand Mills, Tirisfal Glades' largest milling and agricultural operation. When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, the aristocratic Agamand family refused to flee their valuable lands. They urged their household and laborers to take up arms, promising to hold the farmsteads against the undead horde. Coleman and his fellow workers trusted their masters and stayed. Every last one of them died. Raised into undeath, Coleman Farthing broke free into the Forsaken, but his hatred of the Agamands endured. He blames his former employers' greed and pride for luring their staff into an impossible last stand, as much as he blames the Scourge. From a tavern in Brill, he sends Horde champions to the blighted mills to kill the risen Agamand kin and plunder heirloom weapons from their family crypt. He means to strip away the last of their honor.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_coleman-farthing-e5de737c54b4fd6b7d2c/1-0000.mp3", duration = 72.5420408, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:dalar-dawnweaver"] = {
  hash = "4185b6",
  fullHash = "b547f4",
  text = "Dalar Dawnweaver. At the Sepulcher, Dalar Dawnweaver turns his arcane learning against the Forsaken’s enemies. He was an archmage of Dalaran, slain when the Scourge destroyed the city, then freed from the Lich King’s control. Now he studies Dalaran’s lingering presence and seeks to end Archmage Arugal’s madness. Dalar Dawnweaver once held high rank among the Kirin Tor. He walked the Violet Citadel’s halls when Dalaran stood at the height of arcane mastery. The Scourge sacked the city to prepare for Archimonde’s summoning, and Dalar died there.\n\nRaised as a mindless thrall of the Lich King, Dalar broke free alongside Lady Sylvanas Windrunner when the Scourge’s grip faltered. Now he keeps an archmage’s keen intellect at the Sepulcher and devotes it to protecting the Forsaken realm. Dalar directs the Sepulcher’s arcane strategy against the many dangers facing Silverpine Forest. To the south, Dalaran wizards occupy Ambermill, pursuing matters he means to uncover and disrupt. Closer by, feral worgen prowl the woods around Shadowfang Keep.\n\nDalar knows his former colleague, Archmage Arugal, well. He carefully directs efforts to stop Arugal’s beastly creations before they overrun the region.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_dalar-dawnweaver-f99dfee2d5c0864dd295/1-0000.mp3", duration = 76.3297959, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:darsok-swiftdagger"] = {
  hash = "6cf2c8",
  fullHash = "243131",
  text = "Darsok Swiftdagger. At the Crossroads, Darsok Swiftdagger watches the northern trails for threats. The orc scout directs Horde fighters against Witchwing harpies in the Dry Hills, whose raids endanger travelers and settlements. He is also an old friend of Witch Doctor Jin'Zil in Malaka'jin. Darsok Swiftdagger watches the northern scrubland from the Crossroads. The roads linking Durotar, Mulgore, and the Barrens’ northern reaches face raiders and centaur, as well as organized hunters from the sky. Darsok’s anger falls on the Witchwing harpies. Their roosts lie in the Dry Hills, northwest of the Forgotten Pools, where they threaten caravans traveling north. Darsok has an old friend far northwest of the Barrens: Witch Doctor Jin'Zil, a troll who lives at Malaka'jin in the Stonetalon Mountains, the land the harpies come from. Darsok sends Jin'Zil a letter with news of the harpy campaign. The two friends have not been in touch for many years.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_darsok-swiftdagger-798ce1784c292f14088b/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.7714286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:deathguard-dillinger"] = {
  hash = "cf2185",
  fullHash = "0426bc",
  text = "Deathguard Dillinger. At Brill's edge, Deathguard Dillinger watches the town and guides new Forsaken arrivals. He sends recruits to drive Scourge remnants from nearby farms and mills. Deathguard Dillinger guards Brill and guides those arriving from Deathknell. At the town entrance, he points newly awakened undead toward the inn, town hall, and local trainers. Under the Dark Lady's rule, they must learn their way through a changed life. Deathguard Dillinger sends capable recruits to clear mindless Scourge from nearby farms and mills. They cull rotting ghouls and reclaim infested facilities. In doing so, they make Brill's border safer and help the fledgling Forsaken settlements endure the undead threat.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_deathguard-dillinger-4dbe8ed58d8c63708c46/1-0000.mp3", duration = 41.6653061, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:dendrite-starblaze"] = {
  hash = "e0e709",
  fullHash = "2fb6f5",
  text = "Dendrite Starblaze. In Nighthaven, Dendrite Starblaze guides druids who come to Moonglade. As a Cenarion Circle mentor, he welcomes night elf and tauren apprentices. Through him they are summoned to the holy grove to master its rites, from cleansing toxins to communing with nature's forms. When novice druids learn Teleport: Moonglade, Dendrite is among the first to greet them in Nighthaven. He follows the Cenarion Circle's calling beyond the Alliance and Horde. Night elf and tauren druids alike find kinship beneath the haven's boughs, where Kaldorei tradition meets the tauren path. Dendrite guides apprentices into nature's deeper ways. He sends them to examine tainted waters and seek herbs that can cure poison and pestilence. Then he oversees the water trials, testing their patience and endurance beneath the surface before he grants them communion with aquatic forms.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_dendrite-starblaze-dc1574f853bb377c7e07/1-0000.mp3", duration = 51.0171429, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:devrak"] = {
  hash = "5e8cff",
  fullHash = "8779c3",
  text = "Devrak. At the Crossroads, Devrak keeps the Horde’s wind riders ready for the roads across Kalimdor. The orc flight master carries couriers and supplies between Durotar, Mulgore, frontier outposts, and the Horde’s capitals. At the Crossroads, Devrak tends the wind riders that link the Horde’s far-flung holdings. The outpost stands where Kalimdor’s major trade routes meet, exposed beneath the sun and vulnerable to quilboar, centaur, and Alliance scouts. Quick flights matter here. Devrak pairs seasoned travelers and new messengers with trained wind riders that cross the savannah and reach Mulgore’s mountains or Durotar’s stone canyons. Devrak also helps move supplies from the frontier. Barrens hunters bring in meat and pelts, and he helps send them to Orgrimmar’s cooking fires and Thunder Bluff’s tanners. He introduces new couriers to flight masters across the continents, keeping an aerial route open to the Horde’s heartlands. Devrak tends more than beasts at the Crossroads. When the settlement comes under attack, he calls enraged wyverns to strike intruders with venomous stingers and talons. His roost is a dangerous target for anyone who attacks.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_devrak-713550783e4ceccd84d3/1-0000.mp3", duration = 67.3436735, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:eitrigg"] = {
  hash = "bc7729",
  fullHash = "07a1ba",
  text = "Eitrigg. In Orgrimmar, Eitrigg stands beside Warchief Thrall as a trusted advisor. A veteran of the First and Second Wars, he left the Blackrock clan’s Horde after its defeat and lived in exile. Now he helps Thrall guide the New Horde toward honor and shamanism. Born on Draenor among the Blackrock clan, Eitrigg fought for the Horde in the First and Second Wars. The battles and the Horde’s defeat in the second war forced him to face how far his people had fallen into bloodlust and demonic corruption. Sickened by what the Horde had become, he left its scattered remnants and sought solitude in the wilds of Lordaeron. During his exile, Eitrigg sheltered in an abandoned tower near Hearthglen. The human paladin Tirion Fordring found him, and their clash brought the tower’s ruins down around them. Eitrigg pulled the unconscious human to safety instead of finishing him. Moved by this act of martial honor, Tirion swore friendship and kept the hermit’s location secret. The local Alliance authorities eventually captured Eitrigg and sentenced him to hang in Stratholme. Tirion cast aside his knighthood, lands, and freedom to attack the city and rescue him. Their bond showed both warriors that honor could cross the hatred between their peoples. In Stratholme, Thrall’s newly united Horde raided the city during Tirion’s attempt to free Eitrigg and carried the aging warrior away. Meeting Thrall convinced Eitrigg that the orcs were casting off demonic corruption and returning to their ancestral shamanic heritage. He crossed the Great Sea with Thrall to Kalimdor and took a revered place in Orgrimmar’s Valley of Wisdom. Now Eitrigg advises the young Warchief inside Grommash Hold. He helps evaluate new recruits and shares the wisdom he earned, so the New Horde does not repeat the tragedies of the past.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_eitrigg-57927e45e7092d9a720d/1-0000.mp3", duration = 104.385306, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:executor-arren"] = {
  hash = "659b25",
  fullHash = "8bf13d",
  text = "Executor Arren. At Deathknell, Executor Arren rallies the settlement's defense as undead rise from their graves. He leads the fight against Scourge zombies, wild beasts, and threats to the Forsaken. Executor Arren directs Deathknell's defense from outside the chapel. In the crypts, caretakers guide the newly risen through their confusion. Arren turns their thoughts to surviving beyond the graves. Under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's banner, he organizes the effort to clear mindless zombies from the village borders. Here, in the shadow of Lordaeron's fall, the Forsaken hold their ground. Beyond the confused newly risen, danger surrounds Deathknell. Under Arren's orders, scouts and initiates strike at vicious spiders in Night Web's Hollow and hunt predators along the woodland edges. He calls every capable hand to act. Their work tests whether new arrivals can defend their second chance and serve the Dark Lady.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_executor-arren-a4cb5dc6bf85429d2321/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.2228571, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:executor-zygand"] = {
  hash = "4fb161",
  fullHash = "40dcff",
  text = "Executor Zygand. In Brill, Executor Zygand directs the Forsaken defenses across central Tirisfal Glades. He reports to the Undercity's high command and coordinates the fight against Scarlet Crusade forces pressing into Forsaken lands. After the Forsaken awakened in Deathknell, Executor Zygand took charge of regional defenses from Brill. Officers such as Executor Arren and field sentries such as Deathguard Linnea report to him. Zygand gathers scouts' reports and sends able recruits to guard Lordaeron's borders against encroachment. The Scarlet Crusade's presence across Tirisfal Glades keeps Executor Zygand busy. He sends agents against Crusader scouts, encampments, and forward bases. That work keeps the zealots from gathering enough strength to threaten the approaches to the Undercity.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_executor-zygand-b530d14ef491e9f03ff0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.875102, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:gan-rul-bloodeye"] = {
  hash = "601fb2",
  fullHash = "387057",
  text = "Gan'rul Bloodeye. In Orgrimmar, Gan'rul Bloodeye trains warlocks beneath the city. In the Cleft of Shadow, Horde initiates learn darker demonic rites and how to bend voidwalkers and succubi to their will. Warlocks study out of sight in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. Warchief Thrall tolerates them in the new Horde, though Durotar's open sunlight is no place for their dark arts. The cavern gives shadow weavers, rogues, and fel casters room to study unmolested. From there, Gan'rul teaches rising practitioners of fel magic. Ambitious warlocks come to Gan'rul to learn dangerous summoning rites. Those seeking to bind a greater demon, such as a resilient voidwalker or a seductive succubus, must secure ritual components and learn the precise incantations. The summoned creature must be dominated before it consumes its master.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_gan-rul-bloodeye-c4ec98732c826c17b99b/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.0579592, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:gann-stonespire"] = {
  hash = "3fa216",
  fullHash = "3fa216",
  text = "Gann Stonespire. Along the southern Barrens road near Bael Modan, Gann Stonespire seeks retaliation for his people’s displacement. The tauren nomad’s tribe hunted on land now occupied by a dwarven excavation. Gann Stonespire camps beside the southern Barrens road after the dwarven expedition arrived from Ironforge and built Bael Modan. The surrounding land had been his tribe’s ancestral territory and hunting grounds. Dwarven miners drove the tauren from their soil with pickaxes, firearms, and heavy machinery, and refused peaceful overtures. Gann will not surrender his heritage quietly. He calls on travelers to strike back at the excavators.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_gann-stonespire-85d7bc94774a68b6a6c7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.7844898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:gazrog"] = {
  hash = "7eb672",
  fullHash = "d2947b",
  text = "Gazrog. At the Crossroads, Gazrog keeps watch over the Horde’s roads and supply lines. He calls on passing Horde travelers to face threats in the Barrens and search for lost patrols. Gazrog watches over the Crossroads and the roads beyond it. Marauders and beasts threaten the supplies moving through this isolated settlement, so he works with its defenders to keep cargo, coin, and couriers moving. The wilderness demands constant attention, and Gazrog depends on passing travelers to answer trouble beyond the outpost’s stockades. Gazrog’s watch extends across trails where raptors prey on travelers and quilboar clans ambush scouts. He coordinates responses to highway robberies, including the recovery of stolen Horde shipments. He also keeps track of missing soldiers, among them the grunt Dogran, who is injured and held by the quilboar.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_gazrog-b94022f52ebf8d7b29b7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.404898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:gornek"] = {
  hash = "49e14c",
  fullHash = "eb1309",
  text = "Gornek. In the Valley of Trials, Gornek oversees new orc and Darkspear troll recruits in Durotar. He receives those preparing to prove their worth to the New Horde. At the Valley of Trials, Gornek puts new Horde recruits through their first test of discipline. Warchief Thrall's order is clear: every youth and newcomer must earn a place through grit and perseverance. Gornek assesses those entering the valley, reads their introductory orders, and directs them to trainers around the compound. Whether an initiate carries an encrypted scrawl, a glyphic parchment, or a simple tablet, Gornek receives the credentials and sends them onto a harsh path of survival. The valley's arid canyons test battle skill and teach the New Horde's communal ways. Gornek keeps novices from lingering aimlessly, pointing them toward nearby scorpid burrows, feral boar dens, and veteran instructors. Those who survive the training grounds and slay the threats in the red rock gullies receive Gornek's final acknowledgment before he sends them out into Durotar's wider, perilous landscape.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_gornek-61638facf00dd566b6a7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 61.4661224, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:gunther-arcanus"] = {
  hash = "ec1bec",
  fullHash = "ec1bec",
  text = "Gunther Arcanus. On an island in Brightwater Lake, Gunther Arcanus keeps apart from others after escaping the Lich King's control. He believes every other undead remains a Scourge thrall. During the Third War, the Scourge swept across the north. The Plague of Undeath killed Gunther and raised him to serve. His mastery of the arcane and iron will let him break the Lich King's mental hold alone. He needed neither the Lich King's weakening nor Lady Sylvanas's help, as others did.\n\nBelieving every other walking corpse remained a mindless Scourge thrall, Gunther withdrew to an island in Tirisfal Glades. Shambling guardians surround him. He has cut off all contact with the living and the dead alike.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_gunther-arcanus-98bc7739dc1359a769f4/1-0000.mp3", duration = 42.9191837, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:high-executor-hadrec"] = {
  hash = "a2be37",
  fullHash = "d9e1ea",
  text = "High Executor Hadrec. At the Sepulcher, High Executor Hadrec directs the Forsaken garrison across Silverpine Forest. He oversees defense against threats such as the Rot Hide gnolls and investigates scouts missing across the zone. High Executor Hadrec directs Forsaken military operations from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. The Dark Lady’s forces hold Tirisfal Glades, but Silverpine faces hostile Dalaran mages, feral worgen, and encroaching gnolls. Hadrec must strengthen Forsaken control and suppress threats to Undercity authority south of the capital. The Rot Hide gnolls and Fenris Isle occupy much of Hadrec’s attention. Tainted by undeath, the beasts have overrun the Dead Fields and the shores of Lake Lordamere, threatening Forsaken patrols. Hadrec sends agents to search ruined ferries and farmsteads for clues, learn what empowers the gnolls, and prepare a strike against their island stronghold.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_high-executor-hadrec-46e779909d5560cd832a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 57.9657143, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:islen-waterseer"] = {
  hash = "442247",
  fullHash = "dc5695",
  text = "Islen Waterseer. Beside the Tidus Stair, respected tauren shaman Islen Waterseer guides Horde initiates through the trials of water. She lives by a quiet fishing hut and teaches shamans to attune to water spirits as they seek their Water Totem. On the Barrens coast, Islen Waterseer keeps to the craggy Tidus Stair, where arid plains meet the Great Sea. Water spirits are raw and near along this shore. Islen chooses this quiet outpost over thunderous halls and busy cities, spending her days listening to the tides. Shamans seeking communion with water come to her for guidance. To know water, a shaman needs inner harmony and spiritual sight as well as study. Islen guides seekers in preparing the Water Sapta, a sacred brew that pierces the veil between mortal senses and elemental manifestations. She teaches that water can be unyielding and deep, yet fluid and restorative. Anyone who calls on its aid must show it great respect. Though Islen lives quietly on the coast, her spiritual ties reach across Kalimdor. She shares a close, enduring friendship with Greta Mosshoof, another wise tauren skilled in the restorative arts. Islen's knowledge of water's purifying nature reaches beyond the Barrens, bringing spiritual aid to lands afflicted by deep corruption.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_islen-waterseer-53d0c0cc43f88ccc4ade/1-0000.mp3", duration = 74.6318367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:kadrak"] = {
  hash = "5a62d3",
  fullHash = "4f2adf",
  text = "Kadrak. At the Mor'shan Rampart, Kadrak guards the northern frontier between the Barrens and Ashenvale. He directs dispatches and reinforcements into the contested forest, where the Horde fights the night elves. At the Mor'shan Rampart, Kadrak guards the main route between the Barrens and Ashenvale. The barricade marks a hard border: Horde-held plains lie to the south, and night elf-guarded woods stretch north. Kadrak keeps watch against Sentinels and hostile woodland creatures, holding the perimeter against incursions. Kadrak also handles military reports between the Barrens and logging camps deeper in Ashenvale. Couriers bring him combat reports from the Warsong Outriders, and he directs supplies and reinforcements to outposts such as Splintertree Post. Those who report to Kadrak are sent onward into the struggle for the forest.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_kadrak-c05dc411ac639b95ac8f/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.0914286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:magatha-grimtotem"] = {
  hash = "ba7a6a",
  fullHash = "5f1237",
  text = "Magatha Grimtotem. On Elder Rise, Magatha Grimtotem presses her challenge to Cairne Bloodhoof's vision for the tauren. The Grimtotem matriarch and Thunder Bluff's Elder Crone is a formidable shaman and political schemer. Magatha Grimtotem leads the Grimtotem tribe from Elder Rise, with her own retinue and bodyguards. An arranged union brought her authority, then her mate died in a climbing accident. Her reclusive tribe follows her as its political and spiritual leader. Magatha preaches tauren dominance, against Cairne Bloodhoof's vision. She sees other mortal races as intruders on Kalimdor, to be eradicated or swept aside. Though Magatha openly disdains other races, she was among the first to argue that the Forsaken should join the Horde. She says the tauren can teach the undead spiritual balance and help them reclaim their humanity. Beneath Thunder Bluff, she also works directly with the Royal Apothecary Society. There she consults figures such as Apothecary Zamah about practical alchemy and arcane relics.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_magatha-grimtotem-32b02e37b293c59b2d65/1-0000.mp3", duration = 61.2571429, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:magistrate-sevren"] = {
  hash = "3a159d",
  fullHash = "8ad99e",
  text = "Magistrate Sevren. In Brill, Magistrate Sevren directs the settlement’s defense and sends newcomers to steady the lands around the Undercity. From Brill’s town hall, Magistrate Sevren directs civil and strategic affairs north of the Undercity. New Forsaken arrive in Tirisfal Glades to find local troubles waiting. Sevren sends them to restore order, secure ruined places, and suppress threats in the surrounding hills. The dead of Tirisfal and their burial grounds are chief concerns for Magistrate Sevren. Scourge-aligned Rot Hide gnolls, graverobbers, and rogue undead threaten the graves and Sylvanas Windrunner’s growing dominion. Sevren seeks to reclaim ancestral tombs such as the Agamand Family Crypt. He also keeps deserters and uncooperative forces from undermining Forsaken authority.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_magistrate-sevren-aa725a59fa9eb63c90a6/1-0000.mp3", duration = 47.9869388, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:mangletooth"] = {
  hash = "89fc01",
  fullHash = "3372e4",
  text = "Mangletooth. At Camp Taurajo, Mangletooth faces execution in a Horde cage and bargains with those who visit him. He offers knowledge of his rivals and Agamaggan's ancient lore in return for their help. Tauren hunters and orc sentries keep Mangletooth in a cage at Camp Taurajo. The captured Razormane quilboar awaits execution, but he still tries to sway his captors and visiting Horde adventurers. He urges them to strike at the enemies of his tribe, hoping to prove his worth or win his freedom. Mangletooth knows the religious history of his people. During the ancient War of the Ancients, Agamaggan's spilled blood gave rise to the Barrens' massive thorns. Mangletooth gathers red crystalline Blood Shards from fallen Bristlebacks and channels the lingering divine power within them, granting ancient blessings to those who help him.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_mangletooth-296fe2c0e3efc011c145/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.2930612, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:master-apothecary-faranell"] = {
  hash = "9c1246",
  fullHash = "a8207f",
  text = "Master Apothecary Faranell. In the Undercity, Faranell directs the Royal Apothecary Society from the depths of the Apothecarium. Once a respected Dalaran scholar, he now leads the Forsaken’s search for a New Plague to destroy the Scourge and the living. Before the Third War, Faranell spent decades studying alchemy beside Dalaran’s learned mages. In life, he sought cures, remedies, and potions to better mortal health. The Scourge plague killed him, but he rose again as a free-willed Forsaken. His curiosity turned cruel, and healing salves gave way to catastrophic reagents. His vast knowledge made him one of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner’s most valued researchers in the depths of Lordaeron’s fallen capital. From the Apothecarium, Faranell directs the Royal Apothecary Society’s far-reaching research. He oversees the making of lumbering abominations and guides apothecaries stationed throughout Lordaeron and beyond. Field researchers gather strange venom, tainted blood, and cursed flora across the continents. Each batch goes into his vats for distillation and refinement.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_master-apothecary-faranell-22c51b18d369a0043f48/1-0000.mp3", duration = 64.5485714, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:master-gadrin"] = {
  hash = "745add",
  fullHash = "f8ae4f",
  text = "Master Gadrin. In Sen'jin Village, Master Gadrin guides the Darkspear through exile and loss. The elder witch doctor once trained the tribe's priests and mages with Zalazane. Now he helps his people and seeks to break the dark curse over their home on the Echo Isles. Before the Darkspear reached Kalimdor, Master Gadrin guided generations of his people in the South Seas. He served as a witch doctor on the islands they called home, teaching the tribe's mystical ways. On the Echo Isles, Master Gadrin and the young witch doctor Zalazane trained the tribe's priests and mages together. Zalazane fell under the pull of the dark voodoo he sought to wield, and madness took hold. He enslaved the minds of his people and drove Vol'jin and the uncorrupted Darkspear onto the mainland of Durotar. Now in Sen'jin Village, Gadrin bears the grief of watching a companion become a tyrant. He works to lay slain tribesfolk to rest and end Zalazane's rule. Master Gadrin knows more of troll spiritualism and loa lore than almost anyone alive in the Horde. Scholars, shamans, and the Royal Apothecary Society seek his counsel on arcane and alchemical mysteries. When the Burning Blade threatens Durotar, or distant researchers need forgotten rites, Gadrin draws on what he knows. He can decipher the ancient tablets of Zul'Farrak and invoke Shadra the spider loa, then craft the bindings such a rite requires.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_master-gadrin-cb2c7c256858f7bebd84/1-0000.mp3", duration = 83.5918367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:mebok-mizzyrix"] = {
  hash = "b2c0d1",
  fullHash = "294492",
  text = "Mebok Mizzyrix. In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix hires travelers to gather strange finds across the Barrens and beyond. This goblin entrepreneur hopes to turn unusual plants and creatures into profit. His best-known venture is a drink made with raptor horns, meant to sharpen the mind. Mebok Mizzyrix works from Ratchet, a neutral port where sailors, pirates and merchants meet. He carries the Steamwheedle spirit of seizing every chance for profit. Rather than deal in ore or cloth, he seeks rare creatures and plants from Kalimdor’s wilds. He believes they can be made into valuable brews and goods. Mebok’s chief venture is a drink he hopes will boost the drinker’s intellect. He believes the cunning and ferocity of local raptors come from the horns on their snouts. So he hires hunters to bring him whole horns from across the Barrens. Ethics and taste matter less to him than the chance to sell a brew customers believe works. Mebok also seeks strange specimens beyond raptor horns. He wants volatile Deepmoss spider eggs and rare Blueleaf tubers buried in the brambles of Razorfen Kraul. These commissions send mercenaries into dangerous country. Mebok believes any creature or plant with strange properties can be bottled and sold.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_mebok-mizzyrix-49d0d90a9f919c844419/1-0000.mp3", duration = 70.1387755, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:melor-stonehoof"] = {
  hash = "a9a451",
  fullHash = "63866b",
  text = "Melor Stonehoof. On Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, Melor Stonehoof sends Horde hunters to face dangerous beasts. Their trials across the Barrens and Thousand Needles test tracking and mettle. From Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, Melor Stonehoof watches the plains. To the tauren, hunting joins survival with spiritual balance and respect for nature’s greatest predators. He teaches Horde bowmen and bladesmen to honor that balance, sending promising stalkers to test their craft against legendary beasts. Melor sends hunters after elusive beasts that threaten the wilds. In the Barrens, they aid Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads. Then they pursue Steelsnap, a cunning and vicious hyena in Thousand Needles. These trials show whether hunters can outsmart and outfight central Kalimdor’s deadliest creatures. Those who prove their skill in the Barrens face beasts in distant lands. Melor sends seasoned hunters after Deadmire, an ancient crocolisk in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh, and Frostmaw, a savage yeti in the Alterac Mountains. Each hunt tests whether a stalker has mastered the Hunter’s Way.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_melor-stonehoof-e408812b9bcf7adccb65/1-0000.mp3", duration = 67.9183673, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:menara-voidrender"] = {
  hash = "c6949f",
  fullHash = "5e5ad8",
  text = "Menara Voidrender. In Ratchet, Menara Voidrender teaches warlocks from both factions the dark arts. The human warlock shares her knowledge of demon-binding artifacts and arcane craft from a refuge in Kalimdor, far from orthodox authorities. Menara Voidrender works from Ratchet, the neutral goblin port in the Barrens. Many warlocks in the Eastern Kingdoms study in cellars or hidden slaughterhouses beneath their cities, but Ratchet keeps Menara away from the Kirin Tor, Stormwind's guards, and Orgrimmar's overseers. There, she can pursue occult studies in plain sight. She teaches any capable apprentice, whatever their faction, making her a rare meeting point for practitioners of the dark arts. Veteran conjurers know Menara as an authority on orbs that imprison and harness demonic spirits. She works with intricate reagents and guides apprentices through demanding rituals to make enchanted attire and binding implements. Her skill is known as far as Ironforge and the Undercity, and senior warlocks across Azeroth send their most promising students across the sea to seek her counsel.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_menara-voidrender-59ac5e5d37e3342b1bb0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 61.9102041, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:morin-cloudstalker"] = {
  hash = "c9dc97",
  fullHash = "def469",
  text = "Morin Cloudstalker. Along the eastern road from Bloodhoof Village, Morin Cloudstalker keeps watch over Mulgore. The tauren scout follows trade routes and investigates dangers to travelers. Morin Cloudstalker watches the trail east toward the Barrens. He scouts the road and guards travelers crossing Mulgore. The plains are usually peaceful, but shifting territories and busy trade routes have brought opportunists and bandits near the tauren homeland. Morin's scouts attacked and burned a Venture Co. caravan on Stonebull Lake's northern shore. Goblin salvagers soon appeared by the wagons. So Morin sent adventurers to inspect the surviving supply crates and learn what the Venture Co. had been hauling.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_morin-cloudstalker-c6b2b2fe40416aaff9b8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 40.3591837, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:mull-thunderhorn"] = {
  hash = "a88e3c",
  fullHash = "a88e3c",
  text = "Mull Thunderhorn. In Bloodhoof Village, Mull Thunderhorn keeps Mulgore’s sacred wells and the land’s balance. He serves the Earth Mother and guides young tauren as outside exploitation threatens the ancestral springs. From Bloodhoof Village, Mull Thunderhorn watches over Mulgore’s spiritual well-being. The nomadic tribes have gathered under High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof to make a permanent home, but greed and reckless expansion already threaten their lands. So Mull guides young braves setting out from Camp Narache and calls on them to guard their ancestors’ vital resources.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_mull-thunderhorn-3ea9d1b3d70807cfd7a0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 33.2016327, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:orgnil-soulscar"] = {
  hash = "76e0b7",
  fullHash = "76e0b7",
  text = "Orgnil Soulscar. At Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar watches for threats within Durotar. He gathers intelligence and coordinates defenses against dangers to the young orc nation, especially the Burning Blade cult in the canyons. At Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar tracks hidden threats across Durotar. While grunt patrols watch for Alliance forces and centaur raiders, he looks for danger among the orcs themselves. Scouts bring him reports from across the region, and he searches them for signs of corrupt rituals and secret gatherings.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_orgnil-soulscar-f5e6cb688aadd5c98e5d/1-0000.mp3", duration = 30.9028571, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:shadow-priest-allister"] = {
  hash = "2322b9",
  fullHash = "885d68",
  text = "Shadow Priest Allister. At the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister directs the Forsaken's efforts across Silverpine Forest. He watches nearby threats and guards Lordaeron's borders for the Dark Lady. Shadow Priest Allister directs Forsaken scouts from the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. From there, he watches for renegade humans and beasts. He also tracks arcane activity around Dalaran. Allister's chief concern is Dalaran's surviving mages. He watches especially closely those at Ambermill, who probe across the borders. He will not let the Kirin Tor gain a foothold in Forsaken lands. His agents intercept messengers, decipher arcane runes, and seek the wizards' long-term aims. Allister's duties as a strategist share his attention with the study of shadow. He wrote 'Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You', a sharp attack on traditional holy doctrine. The book considers undeath's harsh realities and the Holy Light's failure to aid those cast aside by life.\n\nSomehow, copies have reached the ruins of Dire Maul in Kalimdor.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_shadow-priest-allister-d856bf57993ef1904d24/1-0000.mp3", duration = 65.3583673, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:shadow-priest-sarvis"] = {
  hash = "e2b908",
  fullHash = "a437e8",
  text = "Shadow Priest Sarvis. In Deathknell's ruined chapel, Shadow Priest Sarvis gives the newly awakened Forsaken purpose and direction. In Deathknell, Shadow Priest Sarvis guides Forsaken who have just risen from their graves. The awakening can be harsh and frightening. Some lose their minds to frenzy or despair, so Sarvis gives the newly risen a purpose. He sends them to put down the mindless corpses roaming the cemetery and guard Deathknell's borders against the Scourge. Shadow Priest Sarvis directs Deathknell's defenses against threats in Tirisfal Glades. Scourge forces test the town's perimeter, so Sarvis sends novices to gather vital intelligence and face trials of arms. The Forsaken must hold Deathknell against those forces.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_shadow-priest-sarvis-b034d861eeee5cbf01ab/1-0000.mp3", duration = 45.1918367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:shael-dryn"] = {
  hash = "409904",
  fullHash = "409904",
  text = "Shael'dryn. Shael'dryn is an inquisitive dryad residing beside the Moonwell of Purity, east of Iris Lake in Ashenvale. She serves as a vital contact for night elf scouts investigating forest corruption. She plays a pivotal role in aiding Astranaar's sentinels with cleansing relics to combat demonic and foul influences spreading across the wilderness. Stationed beside the Moonwell of Purity, Shael'dryn keeps watch alongside the night elf sentinels guarding the eastern approaches of the forest. When corruption surfaces among the local wildlife or tainted relics threaten the land's harmony, her deep natural understanding allows her to guide adventurers through the steps required to restore spiritual balance.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_shael-dryn-22d2737897674d1b38bc/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.6277551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:shenthul"] = {
  hash = "22f6dc",
  fullHash = "da7bc1",
  text = "Shenthul. In Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, Shenthul trains rogues and serves the Shattered Hand. He directs covert work across Kalimdor and brings promising rogues into its ranks. Shenthul trains rogues in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. While warriors and shamans march openly across Durotar, he teaches stealth, ambush, and subterfuge. His students learn fieldcraft and lethal arts for work in Kalimdor's harsh wilderness and unforgiving politics. Shenthul speaks for the Shattered Hand, once an orcish clan and now the Horde's intelligence network and secret service. He describes it as a watchful presence across Kalimdor, investigating, judging, and carrying out its own sentences. Pragmatic and independent of shifting politics, Shenthul reminds outsiders that the Shattered Hand existed before Warchief Thrall took power and will endure after him.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_shenthul-2da54aa9e0da536879fd/1-0000.mp3", duration = 50.7297959, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:sputtervalve"] = {
  hash = "5b5869",
  fullHash = "bd7973",
  text = "Sputtervalve. Under pressure in Ratchet, Sputtervalve races to finish shredder research for the Tinkers' Union. Director Riddlevox holds him to crushing deadlines, and he hires adventurers to steal designs from the rival Venture Company. In Ratchet, Sputtervalve answers to Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union. The goblin engineer oversees shredder development and has found the work brutal. Modern mechanization moves fast, the Venture Company presses hard, and his own prototypes are few. With the deadline closing in, Sputtervalve fears admitting failure to the Union. He turns to a familiar goblin practice: stealing better designs from those who built them first. The Venture Company's drilling operation at the Sludge Fen, to the northwest, is Sputtervalve's chief target. Its latest shredders have interchangeable hands, refined control grips, and advanced inner workings, including the elusive samophlange. Sputtervalve sent his associate Wizzlecrank into the Fen for field research, but Wizzlecrank became trapped. Now Sputtervalve hires wandering mercenaries to recover the stolen technology and rescue his partner. Sputtervalve also helps with strange curiosities that pass through the Barrens. Adventurers sometimes bring him bizarre artifacts infused with corruption from the Wailing Caverns, such as a glowing shard. He knows the local landscape well enough to point them away from machinery and toward the isolated druids encamped above the caverns.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_sputtervalve-df922f3ed2c5b40fb1a8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 85.002449, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:strahad-farsan"] = {
  hash = "cb26a9",
  fullHash = "2a9c06",
  text = "Strahad Farsan. Above Ratchet, Strahad Farsan teaches warlocks to bind demons. The human warlock lives in a stone tower in the Barrens, beyond the reach of ordinary Alliance and Horde politics. Students of fel magic come from Stormwind, Orgrimmar, and the Undercity to learn from him. Strahad Farsan keeps to a stone tower on the bluffs above Ratchet. The goblin port's neutral ground lets him practice dangerous summonings away from Alliance magistrates and Horde shamans. His acolytes gather around him as he studies the Twisting Nether, apart from the struggles over territory below. Strahad learned the danger of demonic binding firsthand. His first attempt to bind a felhunter nearly cost him his life, leaving him cautious and exacting. Despite being human, he has earned the respect of Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind and demonic scholars in the Undercity and Orgrimmar. Warlocks of either faction seeking to command felhunters or fiery steeds are sent to his tower.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_strahad-farsan-1e8dc7e6567a9611c680/1-0000.mp3", duration = 54.3085714, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:sylvanas-windrunner"] = {
  hash = "c2c158",
  fullHash = "c349c3",
  text = "Sylvanas Windrunner. Beneath Lordaeron's ruins, Sylvanas Windrunner rules the Forsaken from the Undercity. Once Silvermoon's Ranger-General, she was slain and raised by Arthas Menethil, then broke free of the Lich King's control. She joined Thrall's Horde to secure her people's future and seeks vengeance on the Scourge. Sylvanas Windrunner commanded Quel'Thalas's defense as Silvermoon's Ranger-General. When Prince Arthas Menethil led the Scourge into the high elven kingdom for the Sunwell, she fought to stop him. Angered by her resistance, Arthas murdered her and denied her a clean death. He tore her soul from her body and made her a vengeful banshee, forcing her to serve the Scourge and help slaughter her own people. After the Third War, the Lich King's weakening grip freed Sylvanas, and she reclaimed her preserved body. She gathered other undead who had regained their free will, then drove the dreadlords from Lordaeron's ruins. She named her people the Forsaken and made the Undercity their realm beneath the ruins.\n\nThe Forsaken faced Scourge remnants, zealous Scarlet crusaders, and wary human realms. They needed allies, so Sylvanas made an uneasy alliance with Warchief Thrall and the Horde.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_sylvanas-windrunner-613ccdd9ce20ee415ad1/1-0000.mp3", duration = 71.6538776, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:telf-joolam"] = {
  hash = "5ffcf3",
  fullHash = "e58bdc",
  text = "Telf Joolam. At the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, Telf Joolam guides Horde initiates through the trials of fire. The Darkspear shaman teaches them to commune with and command the volatile element. Telf Joolam tends the Shrine of the Dormant Flame among the crags overlooking the borderlands. Fire spirits demand sharp discipline and unwavering focus, unlike the calm certainty of earth or the patient depth of water. Telf prepares young shamans for trials that test their worth before the wild embers consume them. Under Telf's direction, initiates brew and drink a ritual Fire Sapta, opening their mortal eyes to the unseen elemental planes. He sends them up the rocky summits to face burning spirits. Those who earn the flame must respect its ravenous hunger and resist reckless pride.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_telf-joolam-864bac321fe7995371c0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 45.9232653, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:thork"] = {
  hash = "b4da80",
  fullHash = "2adbb5",
  text = "Thork. At the Crossroads, Thork keeps watch over the settlement’s defenses. He sends Horde adventurers against raiders and works to keep supply routes open. Thork commands the defenses at the Crossroads, where roads link Durotar, Mulgore, and lands beyond. The town faces threats from every side. Quilboar raids, centaur attacks, and harpies on the prowl stretch his forces thin. Thork calls on capable travelers to meet dangers his guards cannot handle alone. Thork’s watch reaches beyond the Crossroads walls. He sends scouts and messengers north to the Mor’shan Rampart, where they report to Kadrak. The northern and eastern routes carry supplies through the Barrens. Keeping those roads open sustains the Horde’s presence across the scrublands.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_thork-f5b28fbca500ee1159b2/1-0000.mp3", duration = 43.5461224, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:thotar"] = {
  hash = "04d3c4",
  fullHash = "20269d",
  text = "Thotar. In Razor Hill, Thotar teaches young Horde hunters the ways of tracking and taming beasts. He trains orcs and trolls who have left the Valley of Trials to face Durotar’s wildlife. In Razor Hill, Thotar trains Horde hunters for the wilderness of Durotar. New recruits learn the basics in the Valley of Trials, then come to him as they face more dangerous predators. He teaches marksmanship and the respect needed to live alongside and direct Kalimdor’s deadliest creatures, drawing on traditions passed down through generations of orcs. Thotar guides young hunters through the ancient art of taming beasts. He sends them into arid canyons to calm and bond with native creatures, including venomous scorpids, armored surf crawlers, and cunning boars. His instruction teaches Horde trackers to build a bond with nature rather than rely on force.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_thotar-e77994d00f6ad5533c07/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.2146939, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:thrall"] = {
  hash = "e81f33",
  fullHash = "93ac5f",
  text = "Thrall. Thrall now rules from the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar, Warchief of the Horde and ruler of Durotar. Once a human slave raised as an arena fighter, he freed his people, restored their shamanic traditions, and led them across the Great Sea to a new homeland. Thrall was born Go'el, son of Frostwolf chieftain Durotan and Draka. Gul'dan's assassins murdered his parents when he was an infant, and human commander Aedelas Blackmoore found him and named him Thrall, meaning slave. At Durnholde Keep, Blackmoore raised him as an arena fighter and taught him human tactics. With help from his foster sister Taretha Foxton, Thrall escaped. The Frostwolf exile Drek'Thar guided him away from demonic corruption and taught him to master the elemental spirits. Thrall became the first orcish shaman of a new generation. After the Second War, Thrall joined Orgrim Doomhammer to free the orcs languishing in Alliance internment camps. Doomhammer fell in battle and passed his black plate armor and mighty warhammer to Thrall, naming him Warchief. The mysterious Prophet Medivh brought prophetic visions, and Thrall led his people aboard captured human ships across the Great Sea. They reached Kalimdor and escaped the doom falling upon the Eastern Kingdoms. In Kalimdor, Thrall reshaped the Horde from a warmongering force into an alliance built on survival and honor. He rescued Vol'jin's Darkspear trolls and allied with Cairne Bloodhoof's tauren. With human and night elf forces, the coalition defeated the Burning Legion atop Mount Hyjal. Thrall then founded Durotar and its capital, Orgrimmar, named for his father and mentor. He keeps an uneasy peace with Jaina Proudmoore's Theramore while defending his fragile nation and weighing controversial alliances, including the Forsaken of Lordaeron.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_thrall-d99a027bf08a9877a279/1-0000.mp3", duration = 105.900408, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:tonga-runetotem"] = {
  hash = "a0d213",
  fullHash = "ad62cc",
  text = "Tonga Runetotem. At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem watches the Barrens' oases grow sick. Sent from Thunder Bluff, the tauren druid studies a corruption harming the region's wildlife and seeks its source before the fragile ecosystem fails. At the Crossroads, Tonga Runetotem studies the Barrens' changing land. His elders in Thunder Bluff sent him from Mulgore, and he knows the dry savannah well. Where travelers see scrub and predators, Tonga watches for signs of the land's health. Lately, those signs have turned troubling. He seeks travelers who can help him investigate the scattered oases, the heart of life across the savannah. Tonga bears the Runetotem clan name and the druidic heritage championed by Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. Hamuul keeps ties with the Cenarion Circle and studies in Moonglade's sacred groves, while scouts like Tonga serve on the frontier. Tonga draws on Moonglade's botanical wisdom to prepare healing salves and counter poisons. His work puts the young tauren druidic tradition to use within the fledgling Horde.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_tonga-runetotem-375f2bbdfeb9fac39fdc/1-0000.mp3", duration = 62.0669388, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:turak-runetotem"] = {
  hash = "80cfa9",
  fullHash = "4972f2",
  text = "Turak Runetotem. In Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem guides young tauren toward nature and balance. From the Hall of Elders on Elder Rise, he assists Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and leads novices through trials to commune with spirits and master animal forms. In the Hall of Elders atop Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise, Turak Runetotem guides those who seek the druid’s path. He assists Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem in bringing the ancient druidic arts back among the tauren. Turak teaches that a druid honors the Earthmother’s will. Strength of body must rest upon spiritual respect and harmony with nature. When fledgling druids are ready for animal forms, Turak sends them into the wider world. He teaches them to join the Cenarion Circle and travel by teleportation across Kalimdor to Moonglade. Turak remembers his own first communion with the Great Bear Spirit as bewildering and intense. To test his students’ courage, he sends them to face Lunaclaw and win the strength of body and heart required for the Path of the Claw. Turak teaches more than the primal forms of combat. He sends his disciples to Dendrite Starblaze to study poison, and Dendrite sends them to help animals poisoned near the Crossroads. Even Turak is surprised by the rash of poisonings.\n\nTurak also guides novices through arduous rites beneath the tides, where they awaken their aquatic form. These trials shape them into protectors able to heal Azeroth’s deepest wounds.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_turak-runetotem-a8bb6a2760d409276902/1-0000.mp3", duration = 89.4432653, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:varimathras"] = {
  hash = "be061f",
  fullHash = "fd95ea",
  text = "Varimathras. In the Royal Quarter, Varimathras advises Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and commands her forces. After defeat in Lordaeron's civil war, he pledged himself to the Banshee Queen and now serves at her right hand. Before the Third War, Kil'jaeden sent Varimathras and his fellow dreadlords to guard the Lich King. They were to ensure Ner'zhul's spirit served the Legion's plans. With his brothers Detheroc and Balnazzar, Varimathras oversaw the Scourge in Lordaeron while Archimonde invaded Kalimdor.\n\nThe Legion fell at Mount Hyjal, but the three dreadlords stayed entrenched in the Capital City's ruins. They learned of their master's defeat only when Prince Arthas returned and drove them into hiding. As the Lich King's hold over his undead weakened, Varimathras tried to make the newly freed banshee Sylvanas Windrunner serve the dreadlords' new regime. Sylvanas refused and rallied liberated undead to destroy his outpost. Facing execution, Varimathras begged for his life and offered tactical secrets, including knowledge of his brothers' fortifications. Sylvanas spared him and bound him to her service as a weapon against his kin.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_varimathras-936c077d037dd4dc83ab/1-0000.mp3", duration = 70.3477551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:vol-jin"] = {
  hash = "d0e9dc",
  fullHash = "dd47f0",
  text = "Vol'jin. In Orgrimmar, Vol'jin advises Warchief Thrall while seeking a lasting home for his people. The Darkspear chieftain is a master shadow hunter. Vol'jin leads the Darkspear after his father, Sen'jin, dies on their ancestral island. Sea witch-worshipping murlocs and human forces nearly destroy the isolated tribe, but Thrall's orcs intervene and forge a deep bond with the trolls. After fleeing the ruined islands, Vol'jin pledges his people to the New Horde and brings them across the Great Sea to Kalimdor. The Darkspear settle in Durotar, but Zalazane's betrayal on the Echo Isles drives many refugees to the mainland at Sen'jin Village. Vol'jin spends much of his time in Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar, giving Thrall his strategic counsel and shadow hunter skill. From the orcish capital, he watches over the young Horde and works to reclaim his people's lands.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_vol-jin-f08a24f4fd477a17ed49/1-0000.mp3", duration = 51.9314286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["npc:yaw-sharpmane"] = {
  hash = "b315d3",
  fullHash = "c0c82e",
  text = "Yaw Sharpmane. Bloodhoof Village is where Yaw Sharpmane teaches young tauren hunters. He shows them how to track, survive, and tame Mulgore's wild beasts. Yaw Sharpmane teaches marksmanship, tracking, and survival in Bloodhoof Village. Young hunters who have proven themselves in Red Cloud Mesa come to him to hone their skills before they venture onto Mulgore's wider plains. Yaw Sharpmane guides new hunters through the ancient rite of taming wild beasts. He asks them to bond with Mulgore's native animals, testing their patience and respect for nature's balance. Then he teaches them to care for and train a lasting companion.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_npc_yaw-sharpmane-bb1233ffe5785145acd8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 37.5902041, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:agama-gor"] = {
  hash = "979eca",
  fullHash = "dda521",
  text = "Agama'gor. Agama'gor stands north of the road from Camp Taurajo toward Mulgore. Bristleback quilboar hold this encampment in the southern Barrens, keeping pressure on the nearby Horde outpost. Agama'gor is a Bristleback stronghold in the southern Barrens. Its huts, brambles, and crude totems lie close to Camp Taurajo. The quilboar threaten travelers moving between the Barrens and Mulgore’s grassy hills, and Horde scouts and hunters fight to contain them. Bristleback quilboar in Agama'gor carry crimson stones called Blood Shards. Mangletooth, an exiled quilboar held captive at Camp Taurajo, seeks these stones because of ancient beliefs about Agamaggan’s sacred essence. Horde adventurers raid the encampment for shards and trade them to Mangletooth for tribal charms.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_agama-gor-a53bdb22b2557e17bf88/1-0000.mp3", duration = 43.52, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:agamand-family-crypt"] = {
  hash = "21e127",
  fullHash = "21e127",
  text = "Agamand Family Crypt. The Scourge has seized the Agamand Family Crypt just north of Agamand Mills. Once the resting place of Tirisfal's wealthy farming dynasty, its tombs now hold ancestors raised by Captain Dargol as mindless terrors. The Agamand family once held broad estates across northern Tirisfal Glades. Their ancestors rest in a hillside crypt, until the Plague ruined the kingdom and Captain Dargol seized the tombs for the Scourge.\n\nThrough dark necromancy, Dargol awakened the Agamand dead as vengeful skeletons and apparitions. Their restless forms make the family burial ground a Scourge foothold beside Forsaken territory.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_agamand-family-crypt-36d7a420518d68756856/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.6277551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:agamand-mills"] = {
  hash = "6bc02f",
  fullHash = "ae495b",
  text = "Agamand Mills. Across northern Tirisfal, Agamand Mills now shelter the Scourge’s strongest hold in the region. The wealthy Agamand dynasty once ruled this farm and milling estate. The Agamand family built an estate around a vast network of mills in northern Tirisfal. When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron during the Third War, patriarch Gregor Agamand refused to flee. He fortified the compound and persuaded retainers and laborers to stand with him. Their stores and stone walls might have held, but their youngest son, Devlin Agamand, betrayed them.\n\nDevlin slaughtered the watchmen and let the walking dead into the sleeping quarters. The defenders were crippled from within before they fell. The family joined the mindless ranks of the undead. Agamand Mills are the Scourge’s strongest hold in Tirisfal Glades and a direct threat to the Forsaken realm. Rotting windmills turn above fields crawling with wights, zombies, and skeletal horrors. Beneath the estate, Captain Dargol commands the garrison from the Agamand Family Crypt. There he practices necromancy, reanimating generations of Agamand ancestors.\n\nFrom Brill, Magistrate Sevren and the Deathguards fight to clear the mills and purge the Scourge before it can march on the Undercity.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_agamand-mills-664f8bdebdde2d44632c/1-0000.mp3", duration = 76.3559184, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:ambermill"] = {
  hash = "296001",
  fullHash = "296001",
  text = "Ambermill. In southeastern Silverpine Forest, Ambermill's wizards hold a fortified outpost southwest of Lordamere Lake. Once a quiet lumber village, it now shelters surviving wizards and apprentices from Dalaran as they resist the Forsaken to the south. Before the Third War, Ambermill was a quiet lumber town. After Lordaeron fell, surviving wizards of the Kirin Tor moved in and fortified it. Now Dalaran spellscribes, conjurors, and apprentices patrol its buildings and stables. They hold this forward redoubt against the undead.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_ambermill-b40b112597aea7be9786/1-0000.mp3", duration = 32.3918367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:apothecarium"] = {
  hash = "47efe4",
  fullHash = "7c44c2",
  text = "Apothecarium. In the Undercity’s southwest quarter, the Apothecarium drives the Royal Apothecary Society’s work. Under Master Apothecary Faranell, Forsaken alchemists pursue plagues, toxins, and engineered horrors for Lady Sylvanas’s campaign against the living and the Scourge. Vats, dissection tables, and chemical fumes fill the Apothecarium’s southwestern terrace. Master Apothecary Faranell leads the Royal Apothecary Society’s work there, studying mortality and rot. Alchemists and surgeons experiment with tissue grafts and vivisection, then assemble mighty abominations. Lady Sylvanas Windrunner has charged them with making a plague to eradicate both the Scourge and the lingering human presence across Lordaeron. Alchemists and herbalists come to this quarter from across the Horde in the Eastern Kingdoms. Initiates and masters gather beside toxic canals to distill concoctions and study botanical blights. They also seek counsel from master practitioners.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_apothecarium-bc23c10046fc607bfeb0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 57.7567347, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:bael-dun-digsite"] = {
  hash = "1da3fe",
  fullHash = "6d63a9",
  text = "Bael'dun Digsite. Dwarven prospectors dig into the western hills of Mulgore at Bael'dun Digsite. Their search for ancient Titan relics has brought them against the tauren, who see the work as an insult to the Earth Mother. Dwarven prospectors cut into the mountain slopes of western Mulgore. Their camp marks the southernmost reach of the Explorers' League expedition based at Bael Modan in the southern Barrens. They seek ancient Titan relics buried beneath the plains, bringing picks, shovels, and blasting powder. They heed neither borders nor the spiritual traditions of the newly settled tribes. The Bloodhoof tribe sees the digging as an assault on the Earth Mother. Baine Bloodhoof urged caution and warned the dwarves to leave, but they would not abandon their trenches. With diplomacy failed, the tauren resolved to break the expedition's tools and drive out the miners before their work cuts deeper into Mulgore's sacred earth.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_bael-dun-digsite-902df246080fd7269d29/1-0000.mp3", duration = 51.6179592, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:bael-dun-keep"] = {
  hash = "6ce2f8",
  fullHash = "ccb0fa",
  text = "Bael'dun Keep. Dwarven forces hold Bael'dun Keep above the Bael Modan excavation in the southern Barrens. Under General Twinbraid, this imposing fortification anchors the Alliance's controversial presence in the region and brings it into violent conflict with the surrounding Horde territories. Bael'dun Keep rises over the Bael Modan excavation as the fortified military heart of Ironforge's presence in the southern Barrens. Dwarven architect Haggis Boatmurder designed the stronghold to protect the Prospectors and archaeologists searching the trenches for ancient titan artifacts. Ironworks and artillery arm its garrison, which keeps a vigilant watch, secures dwarven supply lines, and projects Alliance military power into Kalimdor's heartland. The keep and its adjoining digsite displaced the local Stonespire tribe of tauren from their ancestral home. Bael'dun remains a flashpoint in the Barrens, and nearby Horde outposts see it as a flagrant military intrusion. Gann Stonespire wages a personal war of vengeance against the invaders. Aggrieved tauren, opportunistic scouts, and suspicious outposts such as Camp Taurajo keep the fortress under threat of raids and sabotage.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_bael-dun-keep-a81bfdb115c4c667d5e6/1-0000.mp3", duration = 66.0636735, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:bael-modan"] = {
  hash = "2c2c97",
  fullHash = "2c2c97",
  text = "Bael Modan. Dwarven crews blast into the red earth at Bael Modan, searching for Titan relics. Their fortified outpost has driven the Stonespire tauren from their sacred land and kindled a bitter fight. Bael Modan's walls guard Bael'dun Keep, siege cannons, gyrocopter landing pads, and a deep excavation pit. Dwarven prospectors came to Kalimdor convinced an ancient Titan facility lay beneath the red earth. Their blasting tore through sacred ground of the Stonespire tauren. The expedition answered no call to negotiate. Gunfire and explosives drove the tribe from its ancestral lands, leaving survivors scattered and vengeful.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_bael-modan-16dffecf76bc3f5b6782/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.444898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:balnir-farmstead"] = {
  hash = "542d38",
  fullHash = "3e7fe2",
  text = "Balnir Farmstead. In eastern Tirisfal, Balnir Farmstead lies ruined just behind the Bulwark. Once worked by the Balnir family, the estate now draws Scourge slipping past the defenses. Snapdragons still bloom in the garden where the Balnir family worked their homestead for generations. During the Third War, the Scourge swept through Lordaeron and overran the farm. Its people were lost, and the buildings now rot among eastern Tirisfal’s hills. Mindless Scourge slip past the Bulwark and gather among the farmstead’s ruins. Forsaken deathguards watch the grounds warily. Meanwhile, Undercity magi gather surviving snapdragons from the garden to learn how deeply plague corruption has reached into the soil.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_balnir-farmstead-605ebac07065f44bec91/1-0000.mp3", duration = 41.9004082, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:bandarion-keep"] = {
  hash = "99d14c",
  fullHash = "0a01e3",
  text = "Bandarion Keep. At Bandarion Keep, defenders watch the coast and the woodland for danger. Near the Whispering Forest, the outpost bears Garek Bandarion’s name and is bound to Tyr's Watch. Bandarion Keep guards western Tirisfal Glades near the Whispering Forest. Named for Garek Bandarion, the stronghold is closely bound to Tyr's Watch. Quartermaster Jorin Croge works to keep the garrison supplied. Yet the keep lies far from the courtyards of the Undercity. Threats press Bandarion Keep from several directions. Vile Fin murlocs raid the nearby waters, while the Scarlet Crusade tests the defenders in skirmishes. Mindless Scourge thralls wander through the gloom. Some paladins have struggled to accept their unlife as Forsaken and have fallen to madness. They turn their weapons against their own kindred.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_bandarion-keep-c9df574b67a10c0be195/1-0000.mp3", duration = 52.1142857, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:beren-s-peril"] = {
  hash = "7fba1d",
  fullHash = "7fba1d",
  text = "Beren's Peril. At Beren's Peril, Scourge loyal to Thule Ravenclaw gather in the hills southwest of Ambermill and threaten the Forsaken. High in the crags southwest of Ambermill, a cave and mountain path lie hidden from the main road. Since the Third War, rogue Scourge have fortified the refuge under the renegade necromancer Thule Ravenclaw. They refused to serve the Dark Lady or flee north.\n\nRavenclaw's regents, guardians, and drudgers gathered in secret to prepare an assault on the Forsaken base at the Sepulcher. Forsaken scouts found them, and the quiet cliffs became a warzone. Now Horde fighters move against the undead before they can attack.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_beren-s-peril-881914fb7eb61a71c0e0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 40.4114286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:blackthorn-ridge"] = {
  hash = "04cac5",
  fullHash = "04cac5",
  text = "Blackthorn Ridge. At Blackthorn Ridge, Razormane quilboar guard the southern Barrens north of Razorfen Kraul. Brine, an orc shaman, keeps watch from a camp above a pool of unusually pure mountain water. Blackthorn Ridge rises beside Razorfen Kraul, its slopes crowded with dense thickets of sharp briars. The Razormane quilboar claim the ground as ancestral territory, using the thorny barriers to ambush outsiders and skirmish across the southern Barrens. Travelers seek out the ridge despite the danger, drawn to Brine, a hermit orc shaman. His camp sits above a spring famed across Kalimdor for its clear, spiritually pure water.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_blackthorn-ridge-89e20b8ecc8188a10a09/1-0000.mp3", duration = 38.3216327, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:bladefist-bay"] = {
  hash = "b75c90",
  fullHash = "0461f5",
  text = "Bladefist Bay. Bladefist Bay opens onto the Great Sea along eastern Durotar, just beyond Orgrimmar's gates. Craggy bluffs rise above its shore, with Azshara's southern coast across the water. Bladefist Bay meets the Great Sea along Durotar's northeastern edge. Rocky cliffs rise above its treacherous surf, just east of Orgrimmar, the Horde capital. Across the water to the north, Azshara's ancient red cliffs and ruins mark the far shore. The bay forms a boundary between Durotar and the open sea. Kargath Bladefist gave the bay its name. Chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan, he severed his own hand and replaced it with a blade during the old Horde's trials on Draenor. Skull Rock lies nearby, where cultists and hidden rogue networks work in the shadows. The coast recalls the fierce, ruthless legacy of the clan's chieftain.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_bladefist-bay-f258510606f0cb125bf1/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.9795918, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:bloodhoof-village"] = {
  hash = "0fb75e",
  fullHash = "7cfa15",
  text = "Bloodhoof Village. At Bloodhoof Village beside Stonebull Lake, young tauren prepare for the road to Thunder Bluff. Baine Bloodhoof leads them, while the village tends Mulgore’s defense, trade, and rites. Beside Stonebull Lake in central Mulgore, Bloodhoof Village is where young tauren come after their trials at Camp Narache. They hone their skills here before traveling to the great mesas of Thunder Bluff. Patient breeders tame wild kodo beasts for travel, and the village is also a center of craft and ceremony. Baine Bloodhoof, son of High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof, oversees daily rule and the region’s defense. Braves patrol the grasslands against aggressive wildlife, quilboar encroachers, and the Venture Company.\n\nSpiritual guides such as Zarlman Two-Moons tend to the tribe’s inner life. They lead novices through sacred journeys, including the Rite of Vision.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_bloodhoof-village-91cb952f28067ee108c4/1-0000.mp3", duration = 51.5918367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:boulder-lode-mine"] = {
  hash = "bb8084",
  fullHash = "e4b10f",
  text = "Boulder Lode Mine. In the northeastern Barrens, the Venture Company tears into Boulder Lode Mine for its riches. Orcish banners and watchtowers mark a claim the Horde once held. Weathered orcish works frame the mine mouth, signs that the Horde once held or founded the claim. Now Venture Company overseers and enforcers answer to Boss Copperplug. The goblin syndicate strips the canyon for minerals, gems, and machinery, with little care for the land or its workers. Riches from the mine have drawn attention from Ratchet. Wharfmaster Dizzywig has sent mercenaries after a rumored massive emerald found in the tunnels. Engineers seeking to understand goblin machinery also know that Boss Copperplug keeps key operating manuals in his camp.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_boulder-lode-mine-c0b5f3344e1fd3d013a7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 42.5795918, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:brambleblade-ravine"] = {
  hash = "bd6e9e",
  fullHash = "bd6e9e",
  text = "Brambleblade Ravine. Bristleback quilboar raid Camp Narache from Brambleblade Ravine, on Red Cloud Mesa’s northeastern edge. Young tauren braves enter the ravine to defend their homeland and prove their strength. Brambleblade Ravine cuts into Red Cloud Mesa’s northeastern edge, where thorny briars and quilboar camps shelter the Bristleback tribe. From there, the Bristlebacks raid Camp Narache and threaten young tauren coming of age. Chief Sharptusk Thornmantle leads the shamans and warriors who dwell deep in the ravine, alongside their trained battleboars. For the Shu'halo, striking into the canyon is both a rite of passage and a hard need if the plains are to be safe.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_brambleblade-ravine-a2e9cdf5b733a0b548ae/1-0000.mp3", duration = 38.3477551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:bramblescar"] = {
  hash = "319923",
  fullHash = "2c1544",
  text = "Bramblescar. Across the southern Barrens, Bramblescar's Razormane wage war with the Bristleback across the Gold Road. Thick brambles fortify their settlement. Bramblescar is carved into the jagged briars of the southern Barrens. The thick, sharp thorns make a vital redoubt for the Razormane quilboar and deter casual wanderers. The tribe is fiercely territorial and hostile to outsiders. They skirmish with anyone who approaches, treating all who are not quilboar as intruders on land blessed by their ancient boar gods. Bramblescar sits in perpetual tension with Agama'gor, the Bristleback encampment directly across the Gold Road. The rival tribes wage an unrelenting war for dominion over the southern Barrens. Razormane warriors fight Horde travelers along the highway and repel Bristleback raiding parties, keeping them on constant, violent alert.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_bramblescar-855b237f72c918bf6647/1-0000.mp3", duration = 50.5730612, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:brightwater-lake"] = {
  hash = "4648d2",
  fullHash = "4648d2",
  text = "Brightwater Lake. Across Tirisfal's lowlands, Brightwater Lake lies cold and dark northeast of Brill. Once a retreat for Lordaeron, it now surrounds an island where a lone necromancer conducts forbidden research. Brightwater Lake spreads across northern Tirisfal between Brill and the Scarlet Watch Post. Under the Kingdom of Lordaeron, its shores offered a quiet country haven. That peace is gone. The Plaguelands lie to the east, and grey skies hang over the lake's murky, chilled waters. Withered trees line the shore, where murlocs and hostile undead roam.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_brightwater-lake-c11855c6cd28b3df0510/1-0000.mp3", duration = 33.6457143, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:brill"] = {
  hash = "7657f6",
  fullHash = "194431",
  text = "Brill. In Brill, Forsaken gather north of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Newly awakened undead travel here from Deathknell, joining a rebuilt human town that now anchors Forsaken rule and arms in Tirisfal Glades. Before the Third War, Brill grew under nobles such as the Barov and Agamand families. Then Kel'Thuzad chose the region for the Cult of the Damned's first experiments with the Plague of Undeath. The blight swept through the people so swiftly that the local militia fled. A vast graveyard remained for the dead.\n\nNow Magistrate Sevren leads the Forsaken who have rebuilt Brill. Weathered Lordaeron buildings line its streets. The town coordinates defenses against Scarlet Crusade attacks, Scourge remnants, and native beasts changed by necromantic decay. Brill links Tirisfal Glades to the wider Horde. Goblins operate the zeppelin tower, carrying travelers south toward Durotar and deep into Stranglethorn Vale. Gallows' End Tavern offers shelter. Its cellar also holds captured Scarlet zealots for interrogation and apothecarial testing.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_brill-252e3416b13dc8924d57/1-0000.mp3", duration = 65.6979592, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:brill-town-hall"] = {
  hash = "957bc7",
  fullHash = "957bc7",
  text = "Brill Town Hall. In Brill Town Hall, the Forsaken govern Brill and plan Tirisfal's defense. Its doors stand in Lordaeron's shattered heart. Forsaken rule continues from Brill Town Hall while much of Lordaeron lies in ruins. Magistrate Sevren directs town affairs from his podium and gives orders to Forsaken travelers. Few known town halls remain active under Forsaken control. Beyond the Defiler's Den in the Arathi Highlands, Brill's hall is among them. It keeps Lordaeron's old civic order alive beneath undead rule.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_brill-town-hall-0117ee0e03a40b2d491c/1-0000.mp3", duration = 32.3918367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:burning-blade-coven"] = {
  hash = "4cc8e8",
  fullHash = "17aebf",
  text = "Burning Blade Coven. In the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven threatens the Horde’s newest recruits. Corrupted cultists and summoned demons haunt the old mineral caves, using them as a staging ground for dark magic on Durotar’s doorstep. Dark rituals now trouble the caves along the Valley of Trials’ northern edge. Imps and lesser fiends spill from the cavern mouth, stirring chaos and threatening the young orcs and Darkspear trolls who train here for service to the Horde. The Burning Blade cult has entrenched itself deep inside, led by the shadowy warlock Yarrog Baneshadow. What was a testing wilderness is now an active battleground against demonic corruption. Before demons took root in the caves, local overseers hoped to harvest their raw materials for the settlement. Foreman Thazz'ril ventured inside on a mineral survey, but the cultists drove him out in haste, and he left valuable equipment behind. Driving back Baneshadow's coven is now the ultimate proving trial for aspiring warriors, rogues, and spellcasters before they are deemed ready to venture into greater Durotar.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_burning-blade-coven-9d28d08cbb8ee3a814c8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 63.1118367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:camp-taurajo"] = {
  hash = "5bd430",
  fullHash = "5bd430",
  text = "Camp Taurajo. Camp Taurajo holds the eastern mouth of the pass into Mulgore. The tauren camp offers travelers an inn, supplies, mentors, and wind rider routes across the plains and central Kalimdor. At Camp Taurajo, you reach the eastern mouth of the pass into Mulgore. For young tauren leaving Bloodhoof Village, the camp is often their first glimpse of the wider Barrens. Dry scrubland and rugged mesas surround this outpost and trading hub. Hunters, leathercrafters, and field herbalists find shelter here, while wind riders connect the camp to Thunder Bluff, the Crossroads, and Freewind Post deeper south.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_camp-taurajo-2559cc5e72bd0d8e73fe/1-0000.mp3", duration = 36.6497959, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:canals-undercity"] = {
  hash = "6dbc62",
  fullHash = "6dbc62",
  text = "Canals (Undercity). In the Undercity, green slime fills the Canals between its quarters. The murky channels carry waste and mark the Forsaken's underground stronghold. Beneath Lordaeron's ruins, green sludge fills the Canals. The stone channels circle the Undercity and divide its quarters. They carry industrial refuse, chemical runoff, and alchemical waste instead of flowing water. Faint light shines through the liquid, and foul vapors rise from it. Water Walking cannot carry anyone across. Still, desperate anglers sometimes pull strange, tainted curiosities from the muck.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_canals-undercity-04ff44f39f45a37584a8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 35.4742857, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:cavern-of-mists"] = {
  hash = "8bdf48",
  fullHash = "8bdf48",
  text = "Cavern of Mists. The Cavern of Mists is the expansive outer antechamber leading into the depths of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by subterranean geysers that erupt through the rock, its central pool and hanging fog harbor strange, mutated wildlife roaming just outside the portal threshold. Before descending into the true heart of the Wailing Caverns, travelers must navigate the Cavern of Mists. Thick, warm vapor hangs permanently in the air, fed by natural geysers erupting from the cavern floor into a deep central pool. Though it serves as an entryway, it is far from peaceful. Swarms of raptors, serpents, oozes, and semi-aquatic threshadons wander the ledges and waters, alongside notorious beasts like the hydra Trigore the Lasher. It provides adventurers an ominous preview of the unnatural growth festering deeper below.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_cavern-of-mists-24cb433f0457f5500938/1-0000.mp3", duration = 50.2595918, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:cleft-of-shadow"] = {
  hash = "351799",
  fullHash = "76305b",
  text = "Cleft of Shadow. Rogues, warlocks, and their teachers gather in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. The caverns give them room to practice their arts under the Horde's watch. Below Orgrimmar, the Cleft of Shadow holds rogues of the Shadowswift Brotherhood and warlocks of the Darkfire Enclave. Thrall's Horde honors shamanism and strength of arms, yet its leaders make room for subtler arts. In these caverns, practitioners of poison and fel energy work away from the valley districts and under Orgrimmar's watch. At the Cleft's lowest point, a passage opens into Ragefire Chasm. Volcanic caves honeycomb the ground beneath Orgrimmar, and their danger draws defenders and sinister cultists to the cavern's edge.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_cleft-of-shadow-8e606e156631b611ec7a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 41.4302041, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:cold-hearth-manor"] = {
  hash = "f74b2e",
  fullHash = "f74b2e",
  text = "Cold Hearth Manor. Along Tirisfal’s main road, Forsaken guards hold Cold Hearth Manor west of Brill. Once a farm that fed Lordaeron, it fell to the Plague of Undeath, and Scourge now haunt its fields. Forsaken guards hold the farmhouse at Cold Hearth Manor, west of Brill along Tirisfal’s main road. Before the Third War, the estate was known for warm hospitality and rich harvests in the heart of Lordaeron.\n\nWhen the Plague swept through the kingdom, the family and their laborers died and rose again as husks bound to the Scourge. Feral undead still wander the ruined fields, but Forsaken forces drove the mindless dead from the farmhouse. They now use it as a trading post and foothold on the road toward the eastern glades.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_cold-hearth-manor-43916f57642425ec0d8a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 44.3820408, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:crag-of-the-everliving"] = {
  hash = "adb7a9",
  fullHash = "9387fe",
  text = "Crag of the Everliving. The Crag of the Everliving is a verdant cavern chamber nestled deep within the Wailing Caverns. Dominated by lush, corrupted flora and predatory plant creatures, it serves as the domain of the Fanglord Lord Pythas. Its towering upper reaches shelter the ancient entity after whom the crag is named. While much of the Wailing Caverns is carved of damp subterranean stone, the Crag of the Everliving bursts with unruly, twisted vegetation fueled by the Nightmare corrupting Naralex's slumber. Towering mossy platforms and winding paths are choked with Deviate Shamblers—living plant hulks prowling the undergrowth. Lord Pythas, one of Naralex's fallen disciples, watches over the crag's central reaches, having traded his noble druidic vows for the venomous rites of the Druids of the Fang. The chamber draws its name from Verdan the Everliving, a colossal, primordial plant elemental who resides in the crag's upper heights. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare that grips the cavern, Verdan now acts as a fearsome line of defense rather than a peaceful natural guardian. Beyond his towering form lurks Lord Serpentis, the self-proclaimed chief of the Fanglords, who oversees the sect's descent into serpentine madness.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_crag-of-the-everliving-e50312049b77c4244369/1-0000.mp3", duration = 69.355102, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:cragpool-lake"] = {
  hash = "20297c",
  fullHash = "20297c",
  text = "Cragpool Lake. Cragpool Lake is a body of water tucked inside Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains. Looming above its dark waters sits a massive timber structure erected by the Venture Company. Nestled within Windshear Crag, Cragpool Lake lies directly beneath the towering logging apparatus built by the Venture Company. An enormous wooden structure spans above the water, serving as the vantage point from which Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle oversees operations across the mountain valley. Venture Company workers occupy the platforms overhead.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_cragpool-lake-9b4be49d139897042572/1-0000.mp3", duration = 30.8244898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:crossroads"] = {
  hash = "fbb431",
  fullHash = "04de94",
  text = "Crossroads. At Crossroads, Horde travelers meet where the Gold Road crosses the route from Ratchet to the Stonetalon Mountains. The outpost handles trade, military staging, and travel between Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern frontlines. Crossroads sits where the Gold Road meets the route from the goblin port of Ratchet into the Stonetalon Mountains. Its lodgings are modest, but travelers find wind rider masters, merchants, blacksmiths, and trainers beneath the watchtowers. For young warriors from Durotar or Mulgore, the outpost reveals how the new Horde links its far-flung fronts and supplies. Keeping order at Crossroads is a constant struggle. Plains raptors prowl close enough to steal payroll silver from the guard towers, while harpies, quilboar, and centaur tribes press against the perimeter. Neutral Ratchet lies nearby, and Ashenvale's contested forests are within reach. Alliance scouts often strike near the outpost's defensive barricades.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_crossroads-a0fdaf8c3d8eab06a4e9/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.0661224, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:crusader-outpost"] = {
  hash = "585b99",
  fullHash = "f18f6b",
  text = "Crusader Outpost. From the heights of Crusader Outpost, Scarlet Crusaders watch the eastern road. Their tower guards the approaches to the Scarlet Monastery and stands ready for Forsaken incursions. From the bluffs above the valley, Crusader Outpost watches the eastern road. Scarlet sentries scan the route between Brill and Lordaeron’s eastern reaches. They hope to spot undead and scouting parties before they reach the Monastery gates. The tower also lets the garrison flank forces marching up the valley toward their holy bastion. Captain Vachon and the other Scarlet officers keep the garrison alert. To them, the woods are unhallowed ground stolen from humanity by monsters, not Forsaken territory. Travelers loyal to the Undercity face an ambush near the bluffs. Crossbow bolts and cleansing steel await anyone who comes too close.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_crusader-outpost-5ccba8b29087b08bba8b/1-0000.mp3", duration = 50.2857143, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:crusader-s-outpost"] = {
  hash = "1721dd",
  fullHash = "ba505f",
  text = "Crusader's Outpost. Scarlet Crusaders hold a fortified scout tower in western Tirisfal Glades, beside Solliden Farmstead. It is their westernmost position in all of Lordaeron, far from their main strongholds and deep in hostile Forsaken territory. A stone tower rises in the western Tirisfal hills, just north of Deathknell. The Scarlet garrison marks the farthest reach of the Crusade’s power in Lordaeron. Its soldiers stand with the surviving human laborers at Solliden Farmstead against the encroaching undead. Lookouts watch the nearby pumpkin fields and forest paths for Scourge fiends and patrols from the Undercity. The western frontier leaves the crusaders in peril. Their main strongholds lie at the Scarlet Monastery and far to the east at Tyr’s Hand, so swift reinforcements are unlikely if an attack breaches the palisade. Forsaken forces are massing across Tirisfal. If they lay siege, the garrison must hold the tower alone or face annihilation before help can arrive.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_crusader-s-outpost-09b9109d717505230ae3/1-0000.mp3", duration = 59.3502041, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:darkspear-strand"] = {
  hash = "688187",
  fullHash = "688187",
  text = "Darkspear Strand. At Darkspear Strand, the tribe’s refuge begins on Durotar’s southern coast. The trolls came ashore after exile from the Echo Isles and built Sen'jin Village nearby under Vol'jin’s leadership. The Darkspear trolls came ashore here after losing the Echo Isles. When witch doctor Zalazane seized their home, survivors crossed the narrow waters and landed on this coast. They gathered just yards inland rather than scatter into Durotar’s hostile red wastes, and built Sen'jin Village. The strand looks across the surf toward the islands they still hope to reclaim.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_darkspear-strand-6ee121f548ec9ae9411c/1-0000.mp3", duration = 32, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:dawning-isles"] = {
  hash = "bcbfa8",
  fullHash = "23709a",
  text = "Dawning Isles. Along Silverpine Forest’s eastern edge, the Dawning Isles rise from Lordamere Lake beneath the growing numbers of Vile Fin murlocs. The Plague of Undeath blighted their shores, leaving the islets rotting. The Vile Fin murlocs hold the Dawning Isles. Before the Third War, these islets rested in Lordamere Lake’s calm, clear waters. Then the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron, and corruption spread through the shallows. The vegetation turned pallid and rotting, and the islands lost their former peace.\n\nNow the Vile Fin murlocs hold the muddy shores and tangled brush. They defend their growing colonies against anyone who tries to cross the lake. Bog beasts once prowled the blighted Dawning Isles alongside the murlocs. Since the bog beasts vanished, the Vile Fin population has swelled. The murlocs now control the isles outright, making this chain of islets their stronghold on Lordamere Lake.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_dawning-isles-3545606a0fa93155e8b3/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.9804082, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:dead-field"] = {
  hash = "b2cb7d",
  fullHash = "b2cb7d",
  text = "Dead Field. In northern Silverpine Forest, Forsaken assaults falter at Dead Field, a ruined farmstead. Rot Hide gnolls serve the Scourge there, and the banshee Nightlash drives back each attack. In northern Silverpine Forest, the ruined farmstead has stood empty since its human occupants were lost in the Third War. Rot Hide gnolls now use the plot as a base and willingly serve the Scourge. Deathstalker scouts have seen signs of a coming military buildup that threatens Forsaken supply lines and outposts.\n\nSmall Forsaken assaults on the farm have failed again and again. Whenever the gnolls are in danger, Nightlash, a wailing banshee, appears and drives the attackers back.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_dead-field-04d0daa2179cc5e83112/1-0000.mp3", duration = 40.6465306, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:deadeye-shore"] = {
  hash = "87d73f",
  fullHash = "87d73f",
  text = "Deadeye Shore. Deadeye Shore lies windswept along Durotar’s eastern edge, east of Drygulch Ravine. Named for Kilrogg Deadeye, the Bleeding Hollow chieftain, its barren sands are roamed by raptors, scorpids, and feral boars. Deadeye Shore runs beneath central Durotar’s red bluffs, with sand and rocky outcrops that faintly resemble a skull missing an eye socket. The coast takes its name from Kilrogg Deadeye, the one-eyed Bleeding Hollow chieftain who fought in the First and Second Wars. No major settlement or military outpost holds the shore. It is far from peaceful: aggressive wildlife rules the sands, and Burning Blade cultists from nearby ravine hideouts have been seen prowling toward the water.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_deadeye-shore-f522e80f9e199026003b/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.8628571, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:decrepit-ferry"] = {
  hash = "7557a1",
  fullHash = "d4d968",
  text = "Decrepit Ferry. At Decrepit Ferry, broken docks leave Fenris Isle cut off across Lordamere Lake. The Scourge killed the ferryman and wrecked the boats, and undead and Rot Hide gnolls overrun the shore. Before the Third War, people crossed Lordamere Lake each day from this dock. Local farmers brought fresh produce to the water and sold it to the wealthy lord of Fenris Isle and his household. For a modest fee, the ferryman carried trade goods, messengers, and visiting nobles between the mainland and the keep.\n\nThen the Scourge swept through the kingdom, and the trade ended. The ferryman was brutally killed, the boats were smashed, and the pier fell into decay. The docks are dangerous for travelers along the lake shore. With the ferry out of service, Fenris Isle sits isolated across the water. Ghouls and skeletal warriors roam the ruins, along with Rot Hide gnolls. The old crossing is now a dangerous stretch of Silverpine shoreline.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_decrepit-ferry-4186924cc20a0a0bd94f/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.275102, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:deep-elem-mine"] = {
  hash = "09e55d",
  fullHash = "09e55d",
  text = "Deep Elem Mine. In central Silverpine Forest, worgen hold Deep Elem Mine and its tunnels. Once worked for ore, the mine fell when Archmage Arugal's magic swept through the region and changed its miners. Deep Elem Mine once supplied ore to the living people of Lordaeron. Then Archmage Arugal unleashed his lupine curse across Silverpine Forest, and it spread through the tunnels. The laborers succumbed and became vicious worgen. They left their pickaxes behind and claimed the cavern as a lair.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_deep-elem-mine-948c84080a82520e7991/1-0000.mp3", duration = 29.2571429, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:drag"] = {
  hash = "1a62df",
  fullHash = "4d5136",
  text = "Drag. In Orgrimmar, the Drag links the Valley of Strength, Valley of Honor and Valley of Wisdom. Crafters and traders line its shaded red-rock canyon, where the descent to the Cleft of Shadow also lies. The Drag runs between Orgrimmar’s red canyon walls, where crafters and traders fill the Horde capital’s streets. Unlike the Valley of Strength, with its military musters and commands, the Drag is where daily city life unfolds. High cliffs and hides shade the street, where tanning vats, alchemical cauldrons and tinkers’ gears fill the air with their sounds and smells. Craftsmen gather to practice their trades and teach aspiring adventurers. Their work ranges from leatherworking and tailoring to the goblin workshops of Nogg’s Machine Shop. Merchant storefronts and salvage houses line the Drag, beside the guarded entrance to the underground Cleft of Shadow. The street brings honest tradesmen together with shamans on their way to the Valley of Wisdom and secretive practitioners of dark arts. They cross paths beneath the canyon’s dim, dusty overhangs.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_drag-17a3d6e26219e6253804/1-0000.mp3", duration = 62.0669388, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:dreadmist-den"] = {
  hash = "34a390",
  fullHash = "34a390",
  text = "Dreadmist Den. In the northern Barrens, Burning Blade cultists keep their rites beneath Dreadmist Peak. Red haze fills the cavern they use as a shrine to demons. Dreadmist Den cuts into the jagged slopes of Dreadmist Peak, where Burning Blade cultists gather in a dark sanctuary. Thick crimson vapor hangs through its stone tunnels, dimming the cavern in red twilight. Away from the Horde's watch in the plains below, the cult performs demonic rites, guards its blasphemous relics, and plots to spread corruption across Kalimdor.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_dreadmist-den-8581cc1b9112be2245d9/1-0000.mp3", duration = 30.3281633, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:dreadmist-peak"] = {
  hash = "a09c25",
  fullHash = "a09c25",
  text = "Dreadmist Peak. Red haze cloaks Dreadmist Peak, northwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. The Burning Blade cult keeps a hidden refuge on its crags. Dreadmist Peak rises above the Barrens, its crags swallowed by a dense red haze that dims the sky. At the crest and in the hollows below, Burning Blade cultists shelter warlocks and toxicologists. They poison nearby water and scheme against the new powers claiming central Kalimdor.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_dreadmist-peak-ad1e60e70655f7a6b866/1-0000.mp3", duration = 25.7828571, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:dreamer-s-rock"] = {
  hash = "f71e26",
  fullHash = "f71e26",
  text = "Dreamer's Rock. Dreamer's Rock is a secluded natural sanctuary tucked deep within the Wailing Caverns past the Screaming Gully. Here lies the sleeping night elf druid Naralex, whose noble effort to revive the Barrens has instead birthed a living nightmare. It serves as both a sacred barrow chamber and the epicenter of the corruption mutating the surrounding subterranean ecosystem. Located in the heart of the Wailing Caverns, Dreamer's Rock functions much like an improvised barrow den. Here, the night elf druid Naralex entered a deep trance to tap the underground springs and channel the Emerald Dream into the arid soil of the Barrens. Instead of bringing life, his connection was seized by dark forces. The nightmare twisting his thoughts now spills physically into this chamber, twisting the local wildlife, turning his followers into the venomous Druids of the Fang, and manifesting terrifying aberrations into the waking world.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_dreamer-s-rock-3bec1510965c2ebebe09/1-0000.mp3", duration = 52.7673469, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:dry-hills"] = {
  hash = "4c27aa",
  fullHash = "39a2d2",
  text = "Dry Hills. Witchwing harpies menace the Dry Hills, where greener slopes rise above the Barrens. The Dry Hills grow greener than the dry plains below, on the Barrens' northwestern edge beneath the Stonetalon Mountains. Travelers find little safety among the bluffs. Serena Bloodfeather leads the Witchwing harpies from their roosts along the crags. Their raiding parties swoop down on supply caravans along the northern Gold Road. Abandoned orcish fortifications and derelict siege engines lie rotting in the brush. Witchwing harpies strike out from the hills to bleed trade routes and harass nearby settlements, so the Horde keeps a standing bounty on their feathers. In the rocky ravines, their nests and roosts are heavily defended. Hecklefang hyenas prowl there, and fierce Sunscale raptors hunt across the highlands.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_dry-hills-0269e7c7407a3f31341a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.1697959, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:drygulch-ravine"] = {
  hash = "1821a1",
  fullHash = "59786a",
  text = "Drygulch Ravine. Dustwind harpies hold Drygulch Ravine, where they menace nearby supply caravans. The gorge lies among eastern Durotar's rocky bluffs, reached by a cave passage from Razorwind Canyon or a perilous drop from above. In the crags east of Orgrimmar, Drygulch Ravine forms a sheltered depression and a lawless pocket of Durotar. A cramped natural tunnel from Razorwind Canyon is its only ground-level route. Dustwind harpies roost along the steep cliffs, where they nest their broods and stockpile goods stolen from Horde supply trains on the regional trails. Dustwind harpies are the ravine's immediate danger. Their matriarchs fiercely defend clutches of eggs tucked along the high ledges. Horde scouts often send young warriors to thin the flock, recover plundered trade crates, and break the harpies' hold on the ravine.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_drygulch-ravine-5dac95c22658822d3332/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.3714286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:dustwind-cave"] = {
  hash = "f4b0c3",
  fullHash = "b196d1",
  text = "Dustwind Cave. Burning Blade initiates train in Dustwind Cave, high above Razorwind Canyon northeast of Razor Hill. The cave is both a training ground and a covert refuge for the cult in Durotar. Dustwind Cave overlooks Razorwind Canyon, close to Razor Hill and a perilous threat to the town. The Burning Blade trains new recruits here beneath the notice of Horde authorities. Cultists teach initiates forbidden dark magic and demonology, preparing them to undermine the young orcish realm from within Durotar's borders. Those who enter Dustwind Cave risk the Burning Blade's corruptions. Cultists channel volatile dark arts, including felblood afflictions. Their work shows how firmly the cult holds to the demonic legacy Thrall fought to banish. Clearing the cabal from the cave matters to Durotar's fragile peace.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_dustwind-cave-9f923fa7bf8e3175fbcf/1-0000.mp3", duration = 46.7330612, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:echo-isles"] = {
  hash = "e70f1a",
  fullHash = "6cc940",
  text = "Echo Isles. The Darkspear have fled the Echo Isles, leaving their home under Zalazane's control. The tribe first settled here after crossing the Great Sea with Thrall, but now seeks to reclaim the islands. The Darkspear made the Echo Isles their home after fleeing across the Great Sea with Thrall. Their peace broke when Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's naval forces invaded Durotar during Kul Tiras' attack. The trolls drove back Proudmoore's fleet, but another threat rose within the tribe. Zalazane, one of their witch doctors, seized dark arts and enslaved the minds of his kin. Chieftain Vol'jin and the free Darkspears fled the islands once more, finding temporary refuge across the narrow strait at Sen'jin Village. Aggressive predators, tainted wildlife, and Zalazane's thralls now overrun the tropical islands. The rogue witch doctor uses malevolent hexes, voodoo fetishes, and ju-ju heaps across the isles to bend beasts and captive trolls to his will. Vol'jin's scouts and warriors set out from their camp at Darkspear Strand on frequent sorties. They seek the remains of their fallen and a chance to strike down the mystic who stole their home.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_echo-isles-422c3994e3d5cf18d3c4/1-0000.mp3", duration = 69.0677551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:elder-rise"] = {
  hash = "c25d39",
  fullHash = "a57707",
  text = "Elder Rise. On Elder Rise, Thunder Bluff's spiritual guides and elders gather east of the central plateau. Long suspension bridges join it to the High Rise and Middle Rise. Swaying rope bridges carry you from Elder Rise to Thunder Bluff's main mesas. Tauren druids and priests teach acolytes here, guiding them in nature and spiritual devotion. Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem makes his home atop the mesa. He restored druidism among the tauren and forged close ties with the Cenarion Circle. Nearby, tribal leaders meet in the Hall of Elders to discuss the needs of their young capital. Peace holds across Elder Rise, though political tension remains. Magatha Grimtotem, matriarch of the secretive and haughty Grimtotem tribe, lives in a hut between the two bridges. Cairne Bloodhoof welcomes all tauren lineages and gives them seats on the council. Yet Magatha's presence reminds the city that not every tribe shares the Bloodhoof's pacifist ideals or unquestioning alliance with the Horde.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_elder-rise-5d39eb67c38ba8f776b3/1-0000.mp3", duration = 58.4359184, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:faol-s-rest"] = {
  hash = "ea0320",
  fullHash = "5aaf02",
  text = "Faol's Rest. In eastern Tirisfal, Faol's Rest lies southwest of the Scarlet Monastery, neglected beneath a blighted canopy. The gravesite holds the tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, founder of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Now spirits who perish near the monastery rest here. Before the Third War brought ruin to Lordaeron, mourners came to Faol's Rest to honor Archbishop Alonsus Faol. He led the Church of the Holy Light through the dark days of the Second War and founded the paladins to defend humanity. Faol died peacefully before the Scourge arrived, spared the sight of his kingdom's fall. In those days, mourners traveled the road from Capital City to leave offerings and honor their beloved patriarch. The Plague of Undeath withered Tirisfal, and the pilgrims ceased their journeys. Now the monument lies abandoned and cracked beneath the Scarlet Monastery's high bluffs. Wild brush has reclaimed the paths, and damp mist gathers around the tomb. Those who fall near the monastery or elsewhere in Tirisfal gather their spirits here before returning to the dangers around them.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_faol-s-rest-3749befad834f0aec715/1-0000.mp3", duration = 64.3134694, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:far-watch-post"] = {
  hash = "4a6ad9",
  fullHash = "4a6ad9",
  text = "Far Watch Post. Horde defenders hold Far Watch Post west of the Southfury River bridge, guarding the homeland's frontier. The outpost protects vital trade caravans from quilboar packs and Alliance incursions. Far Watch Post guards the western foot of the bridge from Durotar into the Barrens. You enter a vast, arid savannah, where this is the first sign of Horde authority. The settlement is spare but built for readiness, with an orcish watchtower, a burrow, and siege catapults aimed across the plains. South of the main road, peons tend riding wolves for messengers or reinforcements. The post keeps the supply road to Crossroads secure, screening travelers and turning back raids by roaming quilboar tribes and Alliance scouts.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_far-watch-post-181517461374580ae421/1-0000.mp3", duration = 42.7363265, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:fenris-isle"] = {
  hash = "8e647d",
  fullHash = "8e647d",
  text = "Fenris Isle. On Fenris Isle, Rot Hide gnolls and a rogue Scourge necromancer hold a fortress in Lordamere Lake, off Silverpine Forest. Fenris Keep once guarded Lordaeron’s military outpost on Fenris Isle. When the Scourge swept across northern Lordaeron, the garrison was slaughtered or fled into exile. The dead claimed the island, and Rot Hide gnolls later made it their stronghold. Their crude empire now spreads across the lake’s shores. The Forsaken of Silverpine Forest watch closely, fearing the island’s entrenched inhabitants threaten their northern lands.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_fenris-isle-073a81059c630df4caf7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 34.4555102, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:fenris-keep"] = {
  hash = "ed44e9",
  fullHash = "ed44e9",
  text = "Fenris Keep. On Fenris Isle, isolated in the heart of Lordamere Lake, Fenris Keep now belongs to the Scourge. Thule Ravenclaw holds the stone fortress that once sheltered Lordaeron troops.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_fenris-keep-ad655105f36fc180b126/1-0000.mp3", duration = 11.1804082, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:field-of-giants"] = {
  hash = "6539dd",
  fullHash = "1f246b",
  text = "Field of Giants. The Field of Giants spreads across the southern Barrens, from Camp Taurajo to Dustwallow's marshes. Towering kodo, thunder lizards, and other great beasts graze its dry scrub, while silithids make the plain more dangerous. The Field of Giants follows the southern Gold Road, far from the Barrens' better-defended north. Wooden watchtowers along the road sit largely abandoned, while great herds roam the open flats. Hunters and naturalists come to see Kalimdor's enormous beasts, but the land is not safe. Dwarven excavators from Bael Modan dig aggressively to the south, and a more sinister threat has begun burrowing underground. Silithid hives have recently broken through the ground across the Field of Giants. They mark the northernmost known sighting of these ravenous creatures in Kalimdor. Their strange mounds and aggressive swarms have alarmed the Horde. Korran, a troll scout from the Crossroads, and Ruga Ragetotem, a tauren warrior at Camp Taurajo, urge adventurers to investigate the hives and learn what draws these horrors so far from the deep deserts.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_field-of-giants-cc2152be01b87d48bd3f/1-0000.mp3", duration = 63.9216327, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:forgotten-pools"] = {
  hash = "62332d",
  fullHash = "b640d9",
  text = "Forgotten Pools. The Forgotten Pools draw wildlife, Kolkar centaur, and the Horde into a contest for water in the northern Barrens. Northwest of the Crossroads, subterranean springs feed an oasis amid the dry savanna. Fresh water gathers in the Forgotten Pools, where thick reeds, palm trees, and Laden Mushrooms grow beside the parched Barrens. Plainstriders, snapjaw turtles, and zhevras come to drink. Kolkar centaur keep a camp along the banks and guard the water from travelers, bringing them into conflict with Horde travelers from the Crossroads. Wildlife, Kolkar, and the Horde all contend for the oasis. Deviate Fish thrive in the Forgotten Pools, one of the region’s rare surface waters where they can be found. Their presence hints at deeper ties to the strange transformative energies altering the Barrens’ water table. Horde naturalists and scouts watch the waters and unusual fungi along the banks, wary of what may be seeping into the soil.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_forgotten-pools-fb4f4f7f918cadd009cd/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.275102, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:fray-island"] = {
  hash = "a45c2f",
  fullHash = "9a30b3",
  text = "Fray Island. Warriors gather on Fray Island, just off the Merchant Coast of the Barrens. The rocky islet holds a rough training ring where fighters from across Azeroth test their skill. Fray Island lies off the eastern bluffs of the Barrens, beyond the watchful eyes of Orgrimmar and Theramore. Warriors of every race and creed train here. At the island's heart, Klannoc Macleod oversees a fighting arena where seasoned fighters and raw recruits meet in brutal brawls. The ring on Fray Island follows a simple code of martial combat, despite the hostile waters around it. Warriors come at their trainers' direction to face The Affray, a grueling gauntlet against waves of challengers that ends with a bout against champion Big Will. Here, Horde and Alliance allegiance gives way to strength and martial discipline.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_fray-island-75356a34fdef70b7ad02/1-0000.mp3", duration = 47.2816327, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:gallows-end-tavern"] = {
  hash = "40c938",
  fullHash = "d96eac",
  text = "Gallows' End Tavern. In Brill, Forsaken gather at Gallows' End Tavern for hospitality and fellowship. The town's principal inn offers shelter and spirits, with class mentors and trade instructors in its halls and covert interrogations below. Along Brill's road, Gallows' End Tavern gathers newly awakened Forsaken leaving Deathknell and traveling south toward the Undercity. Though undead, they come for fellowship, trade, and refuge. Class instructors guide young warriors, priests, mages, rogues, and warlocks. Vendors and medical practitioners are here as well. Beneath the tavern's floorboards, prisoners of war are bound and guarded out of public view. Among them are a captured Scarlet Zealot and a Dwarven Mountaineer. The Forsaken hold them for interrogation and experimentation as they fight to secure their borders against zealous crusaders and Alliance scouts.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_gallows-end-tavern-85e77caf99cab05a4012/1-0000.mp3", duration = 52.1404082, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:garren-s-haunt"] = {
  hash = "bf3c2a",
  fullHash = "9cdabd",
  text = "Garren's Haunt. Rot Hide gnolls prowl the ruined fields of Garren's Haunt in northern Tirisfal. The Garren family farmed here until the Scourge slaughtered them and left their home to decay. Under the Kingdom of Lordaeron, Garren's Haunt fed a human family. Before the Third War, its fields gave bountiful harvests. Then the Plague of Undeath swept across the countryside, and the Scourge came to the farm. Garren and his kin were slaughtered. Now gray, withered fields surround a farmhouse and barn, both decaying beneath Tirisfal's gloom. Rot Hide gnolls have claimed the farm, led by the vicious Maggot Eye. Tainted by undeath, they defend their scavenged ground fiercely. They pick clean what remains and savage travelers or Forsaken patrols passing through northern Tirisfal.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_garren-s-haunt-da8549055d9e470e9ba8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.5542857, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar"] = {
  hash = "ed08c0",
  fullHash = "c8c523",
  text = "Gates of Orgrimmar. At Orgrimmar's southern gate, timber and iron guard the entrance cut into northern Durotar's red rock. The passage leads from the arid wastes to the Valley of Strength, the capital's busy commons. The gate proclaims the Horde's endurance and strength in war. Orgrimmar's main gate guards the great chasm cut into the mountains around the city. Towering wooden palisades, iron spikes, and watchtowers fortify the entrance. Travelers coming from Razor Hill and Durotar's scrublands find a grand welcome and a warning to any who threaten the new Horde. Armed Orgrimmar Grunts patrol the approach and watch everyone entering the city. Beyond the gate's shadowed arch, you enter the Valley of Strength, Orgrimmar's civic and martial heart. The tunnel narrows the way for envoys, merchants, and warriors, with sentries watching those who pass. Here stands Warchief Thrall's dream of a secure refuge carved from the harsh desert, where the Horde's many peoples can walk together without fear.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_gates-of-orgrimmar-ad1103d80fafd9bc93ba/1-0000.mp3", duration = 58.3053061, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:gold-road"] = {
  hash = "c08f50",
  fullHash = "6b83ec",
  text = "Gold Road. Horde caravans and warriors travel the Gold Road through the Barrens. It runs from Mor'shan Rampart on the border of Ashenvale, past the Crossroads, toward the south. The Gold Road is a long dirt highway through the center of the Barrens. Near its northern end, Mor'shan Rampart and Mor'shan Base Camp guard against night elf incursions from Ashenvale. Farther south, an eastern roadway connects directly to Durotar before the Gold Road reaches the Crossroads. Beyond the settlement, it passes the waters of local oases and the foothills near the Wailing Caverns. The northern span ends at a dried-up riverbed, where travelers enter the more dangerous southern Barrens. The Gold Road carries Horde trade and military movements between Kalimdor's central territories, but danger follows its length. Quilboar tribes, centaur warbands, plainstriders, and lions threaten supply caravans and lone messengers. The Horde spends considerable resources placing scouts and warriors along the road. Even so, travelers leave the safety of major outposts armed and alert.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_gold-road-dcb826909316720abbd1/1-0000.mp3", duration = 63.0334694, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:golden-plains"] = {
  hash = "511ff1",
  fullHash = "511ff1",
  text = "Golden Plains. Across central Mulgore, the Golden Plains lie southeast of Thunder Bluff. Tauren hunt in this sunlit basin as wandering kodo herds graze. Below Thunder Bluff’s towering mesas, golden and green grasses spread across Mulgore’s wild heart. Nomadic tauren cherish these traditional hunting grounds, where wildlife thrives. Broad kodo herds roam the basin, and hunters tell stories of legendary quarry. One is the great kodo Arra'chea, wandering through the tall grass.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_golden-plains-dde8844fa8082677ec02/1-0000.mp3", duration = 29.5706122, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:greymane-wall"] = {
  hash = "358890",
  fullHash = "358890",
  text = "Greymane Wall. At Silverpine’s southern edge, Greymane Wall bars the way into Gilneas. King Genn Greymane raised it after the Second War, and its gates remain locked to the outside world. After the Second War, King Genn Greymane turned from the Alliance, resentful of its demands, especially the taxes for the orc internment camps. He believed Gilneas had paid enough in coin and blood for troubles beyond its borders. So he withdrew the kingdom from the Alliance and ordered a vast barrier across the head of the peninsula. When the Third War brought the Plague of Undeath and desperate refugees to the wall, its gates stayed shut.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_greymane-wall-fbbd6445c94e4e7bad89/1-0000.mp3", duration = 36.5453061, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:grol-dom-farm"] = {
  hash = "113550",
  fullHash = "fc9bbd",
  text = "Grol'dom Farm. Along the road from Durotar to the Crossroads, Grol'dom Farm raises swine in the northern Barrens. Kranal Fiss and his family work the homestead, despite constant harassment from aggressive local quilboars. Established after Durotar was settled, Grol'dom Farm is an early Horde effort to farm the dry Barrens. Kranal Fiss and his children tend the homestead and raise pigs, while Razormane quilboar raiders prowl the nearby ridges. The farm supplies sustenance to the emerging orcish nation, though life here remains lonely and rugged. Grol'dom Farm is a pig farm, but its purpose reaches beyond that daily work. Kranal Fiss knows the elemental rites and plays a key part in guiding young shaman through their trials. Horde initiates on the spiritual path hold the farm in quiet regard, and seekers traveling west from Orgrimmar are regularly directed here to learn how to commune with the primal spirits of fire.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_grol-dom-farm-ebf1473b80d8bc09941c/1-0000.mp3", duration = 53.0546939, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:grommash-hold"] = {
  hash = "5773b2",
  fullHash = "ed7b1d",
  text = "Grommash Hold. In Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom, Grommash Hold commands the red cliffs as Thrall's seat. Named for Grommash Hellscream's sacrifice, it is the political heart of the new Horde. Grommash Hold rises from the cliffs of the Valley of Wisdom, where Thrall receives emissaries, petitioners, and warlords. Its thick stone halls stay dim and chilly, a choice meant to keep those who attend his audiences alert and sober. Thrall weighs the defense of Kalimdor with veteran counselors such as Eitrigg, while racial chieftains like Vol'jin visit the hold. Outside the fortress, Mannoroth's shattered armor and horned skull hang from the trunk of an ancient tree. The memorial honors Grom Hellscream, who gave his life to slay the pit lord in Ashenvale. It recalls the orcs' freedom from the demonic blood curse and warns against returning to reckless savagery.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_grommash-hold-2675b5d7cf0c6381c7ab/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.3714286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:gunther-s-retreat"] = {
  hash = "f3f682",
  fullHash = "f3f682",
  text = "Gunther's Retreat. On an island in Brightwater Lake, Gunther's Retreat shelters a renegade necromancer. Gunther Arcanus broke free of the Scourge by sheer will, yet trusts no outsider and keeps undead minions near his camp. Mist hangs over Brightwater Lake, where undead sentinels guard Gunther Arcanus's lonely camp. Raised in undeath, Gunther mastered the arcane arts and tore his soul from the Lich King's grip without help.\n\nHe mistrusts everyone and believes the undead wandering Lordaeron remain puppets of the Scourge. So Gunther withdrew to the island to practice his craft in peace. His zombie sentinels attack anyone who crosses the water.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_gunther-s-retreat-2e7189c2ab209625090e/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.1314286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:hall-of-legends"] = {
  hash = "1a8a9d",
  fullHash = "6b743c",
  text = "Hall of Legends. In Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength, Horde champions gather in the Hall of Legends. Behind its guarded entrance, proven officers confer over battle plans and arm themselves with weapons and armor from conflicts across Azeroth and beyond. Horde officers gather in the Hall of Legends, off the Valley of Strength's busy avenues. Beyond its guarded entrance, strategists and delegates from across the faction confer over maps of contested lands and the military standing of both factions. Among them are Chieftain Earthbind of Thunder Bluff, Blood Guard Hini'wana of the Darkspear, and Advisor Willington of the Undercity. Only warriors who have reached the rank of Stone Guard or higher may enter and claim the arms and spoils kept within. The Hall of Legends holds armories stocked with battle-tested wargear for proven Horde officers. For those rising through the military ranks, its weapons and armor mark honor, martial skill, and victory hard won.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_hall-of-legends-2b24f9304833d502d526/1-0000.mp3", duration = 53.524898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:hall-of-the-brave"] = {
  hash = "7d23f2",
  fullHash = "7d23f2",
  text = "Hall of the Brave. Warriors train and gather at the Hall of the Brave in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. The barracks and guild house serves the Horde's front-line combatants, drillmasters, and battlemasters. The Hall of the Brave overlooks the Valley of Honor's waters and training rings. Veteran officers and seasoned warriors teach initiates melee combat, stances, and discipline. Training dummies and weapons line the hall, where battlemasters organize combatants for major military engagements across Azeroth.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_hall-of-the-brave-e6298f40cac5298308fc/1-0000.mp3", duration = 26.0440816, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:hidden-path"] = {
  hash = "cf7e7a",
  fullHash = "40da32",
  text = "Hidden Path. In Durotar, the Hidden Path climbs above the Valley of Trials toward Spirit Rock. Young shaman follow it to prove their awareness and discipline, while its high reaches look west toward the Barrens. The Hidden Path climbs through red peaks above the Valley of Trials, hard to spot from the canyon floor. Mentors send young shaman along it to test their awareness and discipline before they commune with the spirits at Spirit Rock. From the highest reaches, you can see west across the rolling savannas of the Barrens. The Hidden Path also cuts through the natural defenses around the valley. A low pass leads toward Ratchet and the road to Orgrimmar. It bypasses the usual canyon checkpoints, leaving defenders wary that Alliance infiltrators could use the quiet trail to reach the Horde's proving grounds.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_hidden-path-7148be62eb6b132ef973/1-0000.mp3", duration = 45.6097959, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:high-rise"] = {
  hash = "ba8ca5",
  fullHash = "ba8ca5",
  text = "High Rise. At Thunder Bluff's summit, High Rise draws the tauren tribes to its central fire above Mulgore. You find the High Rise at Thunder Bluff's summit, where open winds sweep over Mulgore's rolling plains. Tauren gather in its open-air amphitheater around a fire pit to hear tribal announcements and witness decisions. Tents and wooden stalls house merchants, armories, and culinary trainers, including Aska's Kitchen and Mountaintop Bait & Tackle.\n\nMassive wooden elevators connect the lower tiers to Mulgore's prairie floor, but none reaches the High Rise from the plains. To climb here, take the way up from the wind rider roost or cross a rope bridge from Elder Rise or Hunter Rise.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_high-rise-7039e1523050d8b34cbd/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.3665306, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:hunter-rise"] = {
  hash = "82a031",
  fullHash = "991611",
  text = "Hunter Rise. Hunters and warriors gather on Hunter Rise, Thunder Bluff’s southern mesa. Its platforms give tauren hunters, trackers, skinners, and warriors room to train and prepare for battle. Rope bridges join Hunter Rise to Thunder Bluff’s neighboring bluffs. At the heart of the mesa, the Hunter's Hall is where seasoned marksmen, trackers, and warriors teach the young. Practice grounds nearby hold training dummies, weapon racks, and skinning posts. There, tauren learn to wield spear and bow and work hides. Hunter Rise’s people hunt across the plains of Mulgore and help defend Thunder Bluff and the wider Horde. Battlemasters on the rise recruit seasoned fighters for skirmishes against Alliance incursions across contested battlegrounds. When the Horde needs defenders, those sworn to protect the herd gather here.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_hunter-rise-446021fba20e3560313e/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.6138776, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:ivar-patch"] = {
  hash = "a1fee9",
  fullHash = "a1fee9",
  text = "Ivar Patch. Ivar Patch lies in northern Silverpine, where a ruined harvest hides what befell its farmhands. Before the Third War, Ivar's pumpkin farm was a prosperous homestead in Lordaeron. He employed lively farmhands and servants. Then the Scourge spread the Plague of Undeath across the countryside, and the farm was consumed.\n\nIvar, his family, and the laborers rose again as rotting, feral ghouls. They prowl the ruined soil without their minds. Unlike the Forsaken, they have no free will.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_ivar-patch-b4f3d83017d57f981aad/1-0000.mp3", duration = 31.8171429, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:jaggedswine-farm"] = {
  hash = "809fa5",
  fullHash = "aaddd4",
  text = "Jaggedswine Farm. South of Orgrimmar's main gate, Jaggedswine Farm raises swine for the capital. Its shed, pen, and watering hole serve the Horde's nearby stronghold. Jaggedswine Farm shows the harsh work of feeding an urban stronghold like Orgrimmar. Durotar's red soil supports little farming, so hardy livestock helps feed the city's warriors and laborers. A timber storehouse, a broad wooden pen, and a natural watering hole anchor the farm. Swine are herded, bred, and butchered here to keep the Horde's granaries supplied. Swineherds and patrolling Orgrimmar Grunts visit the farm, though the dry heat can leave it looking half-tended. Wild and mature swine roam inside and beyond the enclosures, sometimes testing nearby guards. The farm stands at the edge of the valley approach to the capital, an unassuming but necessary part of Durotar's daily supply work.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_jaggedswine-farm-15dfdbaaf1f185fbdd26/1-0000.mp3", duration = 50.964898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:kodo-rock"] = {
  hash = "6ab2c5",
  fullHash = "bc5649",
  text = "Kodo Rock. Young tauren shamans are sent to Kodo Rock on Red Cloud Mesa, between Camp Narache and Brambleblade Ravine. The stone rises among Mulgore’s grasses and is easy to miss among the rolling hills. Kodo Rock marks the straight path from Camp Narache to Brambleblade Ravine, where hostile quilboar hold territory. Worn earth circles its base. Its shape recalls the kodo beasts that wander the grasslands, though the stone is smaller than the bluffs around Red Cloud Mesa. For tribesfolk crossing Mulgore’s windswept plains, it is a quiet landmark. Among the Shu'halo, natural formations carry spiritual weight. Young tauren shamans beginning their spiritual walk are sent to Kodo Rock for their early rites of passage. At the solitary stone, novices commune with elemental forces and honor the natural world. Then they venture into more perilous reaches of the continent.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_kodo-rock-1c0457d8c83674deba77/1-0000.mp3", duration = 53.4987755, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:kolkar-crag"] = {
  hash = "e81edd",
  fullHash = "e81edd",
  text = "Kolkar Crag. Kolkar centaur watch the southern Durotar flats from Kolkar Crag, a gorge they have claimed for their raids. Warlord Kolkanis leads them against nearby Horde settlements. Kolkar centaur hold a fortified gorge in southern Durotar. They guard its natural choke points and watch the surrounding flats for openings in orc and Darkspear holdings. Scouts and marauders range from the crag, probing those defenses. For young warriors training in the Valley of Trials and patrols along the southern coast, this is the nearest organized centaur threat.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_kolkar-crag-97b355a6ebea2791d523/1-0000.mp3", duration = 31.9216327, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:lushwater-oasis"] = {
  hash = "09e12c",
  fullHash = "09e12c",
  text = "Lushwater Oasis. South of the Crossroads, Lushwater Oasis is one of three life-giving watering holes in the Barrens. Kolkar centaur threaten travelers who come for its water, while the tainted pools draw anglers seeking Deviate Fish. Lushwater Oasis lies a short march south of the Crossroads, beneath the Barrens sun. Its palms and springs draw thirsty beasts, but Kolkar centaur hold the banks and ambush wildlife and travelers. The oasis also marks the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. Energies from its underground passages taint the pools, where unnatural creatures and strange mutations take hold.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_lushwater-oasis-118fb73d92fc9ccfc5b4/1-0000.mp3", duration = 34.8212245, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:magic-quarter"] = {
  hash = "04a440",
  fullHash = "2ea932",
  text = "Magic Quarter. In the Undercity's northeast, Forsaken spellcasters study arcane and fel arts. The Temple of the Damned anchors their work. In the Undercity's northeast, Forsaken mages keep arcane learning alive and explore darker arts. The Temple of the Damned, built by the Scourge, now serves the free-willed undead. Beneath its vaulted ceilings, mages shape magical energies while warlocks commune with demons. Their work makes the quarter a center of study and occult research in Lordaeron. Spellcasters come here to train and practice their crafts. Portal trainers keep routes open across Horde territories, while master tailors make robes and shrouds from magically infused fabrics. Dalaran keeps academic wizardry apart from forbidden magic. Forsaken practitioners study arcane and fel power in the same halls, seeking strength against their many enemies.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_magic-quarter-9c6fb0fba4b4351a212a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 54.3085714, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:malden-s-orchard"] = {
  hash = "396c8d",
  fullHash = "396c8d",
  text = "Malden's Orchard. Black worgs prowl Malden's Orchard in northern Silverpine Forest. Malden, the human farmer who gave it his name, fled during the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. Its dark evergreen trees grow wild, and a Forsaken scout was cut off from his unit in the crumbling cottage. Malden's Orchard once sent fresh fruit to Lordaeron's towns. Malden, a human farmer, tended the land before the Third War. When the Scourge swept through the kingdom, he abandoned the farm and fled the plague.\n\nSince then, Silverpine's dark mists have closed over the orchard. Its evergreen trees go unpruned, and fruit rots on blighted boughs. Wild predators have claimed the plot.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_malden-s-orchard-7283b8051c9f943e72a2/1-0000.mp3", duration = 41.9787755, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:merchant-coast"] = {
  hash = "abbcfe",
  fullHash = "abbcfe",
  text = "Merchant Coast. Trade and piracy shape the Merchant Coast along the Barrens' eastern shore. Ratchet handles sea trade, while pirates contest the coast. The Merchant Coast runs along the Barrens' eastern edge, where ships link central Kalimdor with the Eastern Kingdoms and Theramore. The Steamwheedle Cartel's neutral port of Ratchet takes cargo from anyone with coin. Southsea Freebooters also haunt the sands and nearby waters, preying on merchant ships and setting up illicit operations along the beaches.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_merchant-coast-2a6d99e05584d0a92520/1-0000.mp3", duration = 29.3093878, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:night-web-s-hollow"] = {
  hash = "b19e52",
  fullHash = "b19e52",
  text = "Night Web's Hollow. In Tirisfal Glades, spiders swarm Night Web's Hollow, the abandoned gold mine northwest of Deathknell. Newly raised Forsaken enter its tunnels to cull the vermin and prove they are ready for combat. Northwest of Deathknell, Night Web's Hollow cuts into the hills. Humans once worked its gold mine before the plague swept through Lordaeron. After the kingdom fell, the shafts stood empty.\n\nNow webs cover the rock walls, and aggressive night web spiders fill the vale and tunnels. The Forsaken send their newly raised to kill young and adult spiders, hoping to regain access to the mine's gold.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_night-web-s-hollow-7e2eb4293aa04d676b59/1-0000.mp3", duration = 37.6685714, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:nightmare-vale"] = {
  hash = "ec7664",
  fullHash = "5d1f89",
  text = "Nightmare Vale. In southwestern Tirisfal Glades, Nightmare Vale lies west of the Crusader's Outpost beneath twisted trees and among hungry beasts. Once a forest haven, it now lies blighted and withered. Before the Third War, songbirds and woodland game filled this valley in the Tirisfal countryside. Then the Scourge's plague blackened and rotted its plants. Ravenous darkhounds and massive vampire bats consumed the native wildlife, leaving the hollow to scavengers and beasts of prey. Ressan the Needler, an unusually large, pale vampire bat, lurks in Nightmare Vale and is known to local travelers. The vale lies between haunted wilderness and the zealous sentries at the nearby Crusader's Outpost. Unwary travelers crossing this unforgiving expanse can quickly become prey.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_nightmare-vale-243b251cebbf3bfaf80a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 47.0465306, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:nightsong-woods"] = {
  hash = "1708a3",
  fullHash = "1708a3",
  text = "Nightsong Woods. Nightsong Woods forms the embattled eastern expanse of Ashenvale, reaching from Raynewood Retreat toward the borders of Azshara. It serves as the primary battleground between the night elves defending their sacred forest and the Warsong clan harvesting lumber for the Horde. Across its shadowed glades, ancient groves clash with fortified encampments amidst persistent demonic corruption. Stretching eastward across Ashenvale to Azshara, Nightsong Woods is defined by escalating violence. The Falfarren River bisects the western reaches, creating a volatile boundary between Alliance settlements and Horde encroachments. Further east, the forest fractures into heavily disputed territories where Splintertree Post coordinates Horde campaigns against the Silverwing Sentinels. Orcish axes continuously clear southern groves to fuel the Horde's expansion, leaving clear-cut swaths that infuriate the Kaldorei. Adding to the peril, satyr strongholds like Satyrnaar and Xavian, alongside demonic remnants in Demon Fall Canyon and Felfire Hill, taint the eastern canopies.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_nightsong-woods-54edf191f37214dc9ddf/1-0000.mp3", duration = 62.955102, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:north-coast"] = {
  hash = "6d0ae2",
  fullHash = "19188d",
  text = "North Coast. Fog hangs over North Coast, where blight and murlocs rule the shore. Cold sands mark Tirisfal Glades' northern edge, strewn with rotting sea life. Before the Third War, North Coast's waters and stony beaches made a peaceful northern boundary for Lordaeron. Then the Plague of Undeath swept across the continent, and its blight seeped down the bluffs to poison the coast. The waters turned cold and murky. Now giant sea creatures wash ashore and rot beneath the lingering fog. With Lordaeron shattered, the Forsaken focus on Brill and the Capital City. Along the surf, the Vile Fin tribe keeps huts and uses nearby shallows as spawning grounds. Ravenous murlocs gather there, among them Deeb and growing tadpoles. They fiercely guard the tideline against surface-dwellers.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_north-coast-e94de68e1cd17d39c296/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.4759184, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:north-tide-s-hollow"] = {
  hash = "5a3695",
  fullHash = "c22800",
  text = "North Tide's Hollow. Moonrage worgen haunt North Tide's Hollow, north of the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Loyal to Archmage Arugal, they stalk the coastal woods from this base. North of the Sepulcher, the Moonrage pack holds a hollow among dense trees. Archmage Arugal brought the worgen into Lordaeron through reckless sorcery. Crude shelters offer little beyond bare necessities. Still, the hollow gives the pack a foothold near Forsaken travel routes. The Moonrage worgen answer to a will from Shadowfang Keep. They are no ordinary predators of the woods. Near the western shore and Silverpine's main road, they menace Forsaken couriers and patrols crossing the region.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_north-tide-s-hollow-793025978d67329ea41c/1-0000.mp3", duration = 40.5681633, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:north-tide-s-run"] = {
  hash = "7fe903",
  fullHash = "30046a",
  text = "North Tide's Run. Along Silverpine Forest’s northwestern shore, North Tide’s Run draws young tauren druids to test themselves in the sea. A half-sunken ship marks the strand. North Tide’s Run follows Silverpine Forest’s northwestern edge beside the Great Sea. Cold sand meets pounding surf, and a partly sunken ship rests tilted in the shallows near the beach. Young tauren druids follow the path of Cenarius to North Tide’s Run on pilgrimage. They dive for relics lost to the waves, testing breath and endurance as they seek the blessing of aquatic form.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_north-tide-s-run-47f184e48d75289d2cfe/1-0000.mp3", duration = 35.2391837, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:olsen-s-farthing"] = {
  hash = "6249cc",
  fullHash = "6249cc",
  text = "Olsen's Farthing. Along Silverpine Forest's main trade road, Olsen's Farthing lies in ruin. Since the Third War, reanimated thralls have overrun its fields. Olsen's Farthing once worked the fields beside Silverpine's main trade road. Now weeds choke the farmland, and broken buildings mark the farmstead's fall. Undead thralls roam the grounds under Thule Ravenclaw's command. They serve him and raid the road, and travelers who stray too close risk slaughter.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_olsen-s-farthing-d92090856170f6fe8cf9/1-0000.mp3", duration = 28.8130612, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:palemane-rock"] = {
  hash = "ba6ede",
  fullHash = "ba6ede",
  text = "Palemane Rock. Palemane Rock's gnoll camp threatens tauren near Bloodhoof Village from Mulgore's western mountains. At Mulgore's western rim, open grassland meets the mountains. An encampment guards a deep cave in the mountainside. Palemane gnolls claim the cave and the foothills around it. They attack hunters, travelers, and scouts who come too close, then fight fiercely to defend their den.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_palemane-rock-e0a46f8920e3381ececf/1-0000.mp3", duration = 23.4579592, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:pools-of-vision"] = {
  hash = "d6c90f",
  fullHash = "fab9a9",
  text = "Pools of Vision. Forsaken gather in the Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff. Still waters and dim caverns shelter their enclave within the tauren capital. The Pools of Vision lie beneath Spirit Rise, below Thunder Bluff’s sunlit peaks. A cave path beside the bridge to the rise leads down into the grotto. Misty waters fill its shadowed chambers, where Horde spellcasters gather apart from the open-air lodges above. Forsaken make their base within the Pools of Vision. Undead priests practice shadowed arts, and mages conjure arcane portals. Defiler emissaries seek recruits for their campaigns in the Arathi Highlands. Whether tauren skepticism or the Forsaken’s own preference for darkness brought them here, the cavern links Lordaeron’s undead with their allies in Kalimdor.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_pools-of-vision-a688918e6d59c1060af3/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.5877551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:pyrewood-village"] = {
  hash = "b685c8",
  fullHash = "b685c8",
  text = "Pyrewood Village. Pyrewood Village lies cut off beneath Shadowfang Keep in southern Silverpine Forest. Once part of Gilneas, it was left outside the Greymane Wall, and Arugal's curse now haunts its living residents. Pyrewood was once a prosperous Gilnean settlement. After the Second War, King Genn Greymane sealed Gilneas behind the Greymane Wall, leaving Pyrewood on the far side. When the Scourge crossed Lordaeron during the Third War, the cut-off townsfolk had no one to defend them. They survived the first wave of undead, but their nightmare began when the mage Arugal took refuge in the fortress above.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_pyrewood-village-8af5e2170d7771e48b80/1-0000.mp3", duration = 34.4816327, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:ragefire-chasm-classic"] = {
  hash = "0983e2",
  fullHash = "0983e2",
  text = "Ragefire Chasm (Classic). Ragefire Chasm threatens Orgrimmar from beneath its streets, where troggs have broken into the tunnels. The fiery caverns also shelter a cult whose plans reach beyond Durotar. Ragefire troggs have surged into the volcanic tunnels beneath Orgrimmar. They pushed up from deep fissures and now threaten the city's foundations. Magatha Grimtotem, a tauren, tried to make peace with them, but the troggs answered with violence. Their tunnels run below the stone streets and fortified towers, leaving Orgrimmar at risk if the creatures keep digging upward.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_ragefire-chasm-classic-3f0a401934fcc04e82b4/1-0000.mp3", duration = 31.2163265, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:raptor-grounds"] = {
  hash = "b479b6",
  fullHash = "b479b6",
  text = "Raptor Grounds. In the southern Barrens, Sunscale raptors claim a secluded valley in the rocky hills west of Northwatch Hold. Their eerie, tool-using cunning and obsessive theft of bright trinkets set them apart from ordinary beasts. West of Northwatch Hold, Sunscale raptors make their home in the Raptor Grounds. Eerie and far from ordinary beasts, they fashion crude shelters, make primitive tools, and coordinate their hunts. Their obsessive fascination with shiny or unusual things drives them to raid passing caravans and Horde encampments. Coins, trinkets, and supplies disappear into their canyon dens.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_raptor-grounds-c5aeefda62705f53c3ea/1-0000.mp3", duration = 36.4930612, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:ratchet"] = {
  hash = "6f9e6e",
  fullHash = "cece6c",
  text = "Ratchet. Ships crowd Ratchet's docks on the eastern coast of the Barrens. The Steamwheedle Cartel runs this neutral port, linking central Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms by sea. Ratchet gives shelter to anyone who can pay, on the dry coast between Durotar and Dustwallow Marsh. After the Third War, chief engineer Gazlowe founded the port, drawing smugglers, exiles, and daring traders to Kalimdor's frontier. The Steamwheedle Cartel runs the town, which keeps strict neutrality between the Horde and the Alliance. Ships such as The Maiden's Fancy cross the Great Sea to Booty Bay with goods, mercenaries, and raw materials. Ratchet Bruisers watch the docks and beat anyone who starts a fight and disrupts trade. Ratchet's docks, taverns, and workshops serve a town with dealings beyond trade. A secluded tower overlooks the harbor from the hills, where warlocks including Strahad Farsan and Menara Voidrender gather. While townsfolk and sailors tend to cargo and goblin engineering, the warlocks commune with demonic forces without interference. The Steamwheedle Cartel does not enforce the moral restrictions found in traditional faction capitals.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_ratchet-ac9216b4a2f9ade543d7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 69.7469388, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:ravaged-caravan"] = {
  hash = "8e2a8d",
  fullHash = "8e2a8d",
  text = "Ravaged Caravan. On Stonebull Lake's northeastern shore, smoke still rises from the Ravaged Caravan. The Venture Company convoy was bound for Supervisor Fizsprocket's mining operation, but tauren defenders destroyed it. The wrecked wagons rest on a rise above Stonebull Lake, where tauren from Bloodhoof Village stopped the Venture Company. The convoy carried mining supplies, blueprints, and equipment to Supervisor Fizsprocket's dig site. Tauren defenders wrecked it before it could arrive. Venture Co. survivors still guard the wagons and smoldering crates, protecting what cargo remains.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_ravaged-caravan-4b02e2c669c6072ba380/1-0000.mp3", duration = 33.8285714, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:razor-hill"] = {
  hash = "169921",
  fullHash = "b8618c",
  text = "Razor Hill. Razor Hill links the Valley of Trials, the Barrens, and Orgrimmar at a crossroads in central Durotar. Its fortified barracks train young orc and troll warriors for life in the wilderness. Razor Hill joins northern Durotar to the southern coast and the Barrens across the Southfury River. Stone-and-timber barracks and orcish burrows fill the settlement, founded early in Durotar's settlement. After the Third War, human forces from Kul Tiras lured the Horde here with a false offer of an emissary summit. Rexxar went in Thrall's stead and stopped their ambush. Razor Hill now stands fortified against further attacks from the coast. Veteran officers such as Gar'Thok direct Razor Hill's defenses against threats nearby. Human marines still hold Tiragarde Keep on the eastern shore, while quilboar and harpy tribes harass supply lines. Investigators such as Orgnil Soulscar track the Burning Blade cult, whose rituals and corrupted agents lurk in the nearby crags, and work to stamp them out.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_razor-hill-28033cd373d0fcccf88a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 57.9918367, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:razor-hill-watchtower"] = {
  hash = "362d09",
  fullHash = "362d09",
  text = "Razor Hill Watchtower. Furl Scornbrow watches Durotar from the Razor Hill Watchtower. From its red stone bluffs, he keeps an eye on the plains and coast, guarding the settlement below. The Razor Hill Watchtower rises above Razor Hill and the canyons around it. Thick timber and iron framing hold the outpost together. Durotar faces threats from Kul Tiras marines along the eastern shore, quilboar raiders across the scrublands, and Burning Blade cultists in nearby crags. From the ridgeline, a lookout can spot warbands, smoke signals, and incursions before they reach the settlement gates.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_razor-hill-watchtower-9ce5653964f10a1f8408/1-0000.mp3", duration = 33.044898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:razorfen-downs-classic"] = {
  hash = "b389b9",
  fullHash = "91ea39",
  text = "Razorfen Downs (Classic). Deep in the southern Barrens, the Scourge now holds Razorfen Downs, the quilboar's ancestral burial ground and capital. Led by the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer, its agents have raised the quilboar dead and threaten to spread their power across central Kalimdor. Razorfen Downs shares the towering, petrified vines of nearby Razorfen Kraul. It lies where the boar demigod Agamaggan fell in the War of the Ancients. For generations, this thorn labyrinth was the quilboar's sacred burial ground and seat of power, guarded by mystics of the Death's Head tribe. The quilboar hold its dense briars holy, for they were soaked in their divine progenitor's blood. The Scourge has broken the sanctity of Razorfen Downs. Amnennar the Coldbringer, a powerful lich who serves the Lich King, subdued the Death's Head quilboar and made their ancestral resting ground an undead stronghold. Reanimated quilboar skeletons and corpses, along with shrieking banshees, prowl the Spiral of Thorns. The Horde in the nearby Barrens and emissaries from Stormwind's Cathedral of Light both see this Scourge power as a grave threat to Kalimdor.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_razorfen-downs-classic-f7cb49ea15debd4e3d38/1-0000.mp3", duration = 68.3102041, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:razorfen-kraul-classic"] = {
  hash = "010480",
  fullHash = "010480",
  text = "Razorfen Kraul (Classic). In the southern Barrens, Razorfen Kraul is the quilboar's ancestral heartland. The crone Charlga Razorflank rules its thorn-walled maze, from which her warriors strike across the region. Ten thousand years ago, Agamaggan gave his life against the Burning Legion to save Azeroth. The colossal boar demigod's blood fell across southern Kalimdor. From each place it touched the soil, colossal thorn vines rose, thick and impenetrable.\n\nThe quilboar believe they are the Great Boar's mortal descendants. They gathered among the briars to dwell and honor his sacrifice. Razorfen Kraul is their most revered stronghold, home to warriors, beast trainers, and shamans who shape the earth.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_razorfen-kraul-classic-7d2addfd4872d0b1c5b0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 43.6767347, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:razormane-grounds"] = {
  hash = "01cd07",
  fullHash = "01cd07",
  text = "Razormane Grounds. Razormane quilboar push east from the Barrens into central Durotar. Their thorn-choked camp marks the front of their unending clash with Orgrimmar's orcs. At the Southfury River, the Razormane Grounds threaten travelers beneath central Durotar's red cliffs. The camp marks the furthest east the quilboar have spread from the Barrens. Captain Flat Tusk of the Battleguard and Geolord Mottle lead raids on nearby orc settlements and passing supply lines. Patrols set out from Razor Hill and nearby outposts, but the Razormane keep replenishing their ranks among the briars faster than the Horde can clear them.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_razormane-grounds-acab143a4aa5e208dd8a/1-0000.mp3", duration = 35.7093878, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:razorwind-canyon"] = {
  hash = "11ea08",
  fullHash = "415ce1",
  text = "Razorwind Canyon. Dustwind harpies threaten travelers on Razorwind Canyon’s road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. The rocky gulch cuts through Durotar, and the harpies make the route north toward the Horde capital dangerous. Razorwind Canyon runs beside the main road from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar. Its gullies reach into the eastern bluffs and west toward Tor'kren Farm. Dustwind harpies nest among the rocks and attack travelers who stray too close to their roosts. With the canyon so near the capital’s trade route, Durotar’s defenders must keep watch over its gullies. Razorwind Canyon’s winding passages cut through Durotar’s red rock hills. An eastern branch runs deep into the crags, through a cavern, and into Drygulch Ravine. Harpies roost on high perches and descend in flocks, so travelers crossing the passes can be surrounded and cut down.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_razorwind-canyon-27d471732000a3b380dc/1-0000.mp3", duration = 49.8677551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:red-rocks"] = {
  hash = "09bd48",
  fullHash = "db05ff",
  text = "Red Rocks. In northeastern Mulgore, the honored dead rest at Red Rocks. Young braves climb there to honor their ancestors and seek their wisdom. Red Rocks rises over northeastern Mulgore, its red stone marking sacred ground for the tauren. The most valiant dead lie here beside their forebears. Among them are chieftains, defenders, and champions who gave their lives to found and protect Thunder Bluff.\n\nYoung tauren come to these graves as part of their rites of passage. They honor the dead and listen for wisdom on the wind. Bristleback quilboar have broken the peace at Red Rocks. They came from their dens and now infest the sandstone ledges, defiling ancestral graves with filth. For the tauren of Thunder Bluff, this desecration wounds their spiritual traditions.\n\nShaman and lorekeepers call for aid to cleanse the crags, drive out the Bristlebacks, and restore the resting place of their dead.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_red-rocks-168af489f7ca5e2bec71/1-0000.mp3", duration = 53.1330612, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:rocktusk-farm"] = {
  hash = "48849b",
  fullHash = "48849b",
  text = "Rocktusk Farm. Swine feed Orgrimmar from Rocktusk Farm, just beyond the city gates in northern Durotar. The farm supplies meat and provisions to the capital, where dry, stony ground makes crops hard to grow. Rocktusk Farm raises hardy swine on Durotar’s dry, stony ground. Crops are difficult to grow here, so the farm helps feed Orgrimmar’s growing population. Close to the capital’s fortified perimeter, it is safer than homesteads in the wild red canyonlands.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_rocktusk-farm-9b45c492b621cc73709b/1-0000.mp3", duration = 26.8277551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:rogues-quarter"] = {
  hash = "cf11aa",
  fullHash = "96df37",
  text = "Rogues' Quarter. In the Undercity's southeastern wing, scouts, assassins, and underworld operatives gather in Rogues' Quarter. Its craftsmen support their covert work. Survivors skilled in stealth gather deep in the Undercity's southeastern wing. Many served the Kingdom of Lordaeron in life as thieves, cutpurses, or silent blades. In death, they use stealth, poisons, and misdirection to defend the fledgling nation from the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.\n\nHere, operatives sharpen daggers, brew toxins, and hone their clandestine skills. Specialized trades in Rogues' Quarter help travelers survive undercover. Artisans teach leatherworking and skinning, turning raw hides into light, silent armor. Tinkers work at engineering benches, while field medics and apothecaries teach first aid. Poison vendors nearby supply lethal reagents for covert work.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_rogues-quarter-b8e0665749a6389e38d0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 52.5844898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:rolling-plains"] = {
  hash = "e7ba6f",
  fullHash = "861b5f",
  text = "Rolling Plains. In southern Mulgore, herds graze the Rolling Plains while centaur raiders and harpies threaten travelers. From Bloodhoof Village, the Rolling Plains run south to the earthen gates of the Barrens. Prairie wolves, kodo herds, flatland cougars, and swift tallstriders roam these open ranges of the tauren homeland. Young hunters come here to prove their worth to the elders. They learn to track, wait patiently, and respect the land. Mulgore’s ring of bluffs shields much of the region, but the Rolling Plains lie open to threats from beyond it. Centaur outriders have crossed the defenses here, the only frontier where they have managed to do so. They harass travelers and hunting parties. Windfury harpies roost in the eastern crags, swooping on stray game and vulnerable nomadic camps.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_rolling-plains-d4099ab22c1878b67c00/1-0000.mp3", duration = 47.1510204, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:royal-quarter"] = {
  hash = "c93eb6",
  fullHash = "15c83e",
  text = "Royal Quarter. In the Royal Quarter, Sylvanas Windrunner directs the Forsaken from her throne. Varimathras stands at her side, and Royal Dreadguards guard the seat of power beneath the Undercity. The Forsaken make their military and political decisions in the Royal Quarter, also called the Hall of the Dark Lady. Beneath the Undercity, Sylvanas Windrunner holds court in its vast chamber. She works for the survival of her free-willed undead and the destruction of the Scourge. Royal Dreadguards watch along the dais, shielding their queen from uninvited visitors and would-be assassins. Varimathras, a nathrezim, stands beside Sylvanas in the heart of the Undercity. During the civil war in the ruins of Lordaeron, he sided with her to save his own life and pledged loyalty to her cause. From the Royal Quarter, he commands deathstalkers and coordinates defenses across the realm.\n\nHis tactical skill aids the Forsaken, yet many Horde allies distrust his true allegiance because he is a demon.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_royal-quarter-b38a9ddad28fbf06db87/1-0000.mp3", duration = 60.917551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:scarlet-watch-post"] = {
  hash = "c70d14",
  fullHash = "c70d14",
  text = "Scarlet Watch Post. In northeastern Tirisfal Glades, the rocky hills north of the Scarlet Monastery are under watch. The garrison guards the monastery’s northern flank against attack. Behind the Scarlet Monastery, Scarlet Watch Post watches the northern cliffs. The southern road to the gate is busy and fortified, but the rugged cliffs along Tirisfal’s northern coast offer infiltrators another way in. The Scarlet Crusade built the stone tower to guard that blind spot. It is one of several Crusader outposts scattered across Tirisfal Glades.\n\nCaptain Melrache commands a devout force of Neophytes, Vanguards, and Friars. They watch the cliffs so neither the Scourge nor the Forsaken can surprise the order from behind.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_scarlet-watch-post-09e8ccc834ea946dc71d/1-0000.mp3", duration = 44.042449, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:screaming-gully"] = {
  hash = "1e60ff",
  fullHash = "1e60ff",
  text = "Screaming Gully. Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean cavern encountered just beyond the entrance of the Wailing Caverns. Bathed in unnatural fungal glow and shallow waters, it serves as the outer redoubt for the corrupted Druids of the Fang and their mutated beasts. Stepping through the threshold of the Wailing Caverns leads directly into Screaming Gully, an echoing chasm where the wind groans through subterranean fissures. Far from the arid Barrens above, the gully is choked with damp overgrowth, humid mist, and aggressive wildlife twisted by the Emerald Nightmare. The Fanglord Lady Anacondra oversees the chamber, surrounded by acolytes of the Druids of the Fang and vicious deviate raptors, while ancient snapping turtles like Kresh patrol the shallow waterways below.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_screaming-gully-4360655d19aa732693a8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 46.4195918, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:scuttle-coast"] = {
  hash = "e4a01d",
  fullHash = "c8e533",
  text = "Scuttle Coast. Between Razor Hill and Tiragarde Keep, wreckage from Daelin Proudmoore’s fleet litters Durotar’s eastern shore. The sunken ships make the Scuttle Coast a place where the Horde scavenges and remembers the recent naval war. Sunken warships line Durotar’s eastern edge, where the shore meets the Great Sea. During Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore’s invasion, the Kul Tiras fleet attacked the young nation of Durotar. Fierce battles with the Horde drove many human warships onto jagged shoals, where they broke apart. Barnacled timber, broken rigging, cargo barrels, and sunken ships still mark the coast. For the nearby encampments at Razor Hill, the wreckage recalls how close the Kul Tiran threat remains. The name Scuttle Coast may refer to warships scuttled or grounded in the fighting, or to crabs and makrura picking through the wreckage. Shoreline beasts and dangerous tides keep casual travelers away.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_scuttle-coast-6dd172f33bc0a0a469be/1-0000.mp3", duration = 54.1779592, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:sepulcher"] = {
  hash = "df597e",
  fullHash = "df597e",
  text = "Sepulcher. The Forsaken hold Sepulcher above Silverpine Forest’s western coast. Once a Lordaeron graveyard and crypt, it now gives the Horde a fortified refuge amid threats across the region. Sepulcher crowns the hills above Lordaeron’s western coast. Beside the western road, its old cemetery and stone crypt now belong to the Forsaken. Since the Third War, they have turned the grounds and ancient vault into a vital outpost.\n\nDanger presses from every side. Feral worgen stalk the south, Scourge remnants wander east, and Kirin Tor wizards watch from Ambermill. For travelers crossing Silverpine, Sepulcher offers shelter, supplies, and a place of command.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_sepulcher-e991fea0e0cc7d347284/1-0000.mp3", duration = 41.0383673, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:sewers"] = {
  hash = "997e34",
  fullHash = "997e34",
  text = "Sewers. In the hills west of Lordaeron's ruined palace, the Sewers open a second way into the Undercity. Bat handlers and travelers pass through the old stone channels to reach its inner rings. The Sewers once carried water away from Lordaeron's royal capital. Now Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken have folded those old channels into the Undercity's defenses. The passage opens west of the surface ruins near a Scarlet Watchtower in Tirisfal Glades, then slopes into the city.\n\nForsaken bat handlers carry riders through the cavernous passage to the Undercity's underground rings, clear of the slow cage lifts. Yet the route also skirts the fortified courtyards. Hostile infiltrators seek to exploit that weakness.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_sewers-cbb35b2b44b283b98c9f/1-0000.mp3", duration = 42.2661224, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:shadow-grave"] = {
  hash = "42499f",
  fullHash = "42499f",
  text = "Shadow Grave. Newly freed Forsaken awaken in Shadow Grave, above Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. Above Deathknell, newly freed Forsaken awaken in Shadow Grave. They once served the Scourge without thought. In the mausoleum's vaults, they recover their free will. Undertaker Mordo watches as they rise from stone slabs and take their first steps into a world that despises them. Then they follow the footpath down to Deathknell and pledge themselves to the Banshee Queen.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_shadow-grave-db671fb311a954885dc1/1-0000.mp3", duration = 28.7346939, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:shining-strand"] = {
  hash = "ec053f",
  fullHash = "ec053f",
  text = "Shining Strand. Along Silverpine’s eastern shore, Shining Strand runs south beside Lordamere Lake toward Alterac’s rugged foothills. Vile Fin murlocs hold settlements in its shallows, making the coast dangerous for unseasoned travelers. Shining Strand runs along Silverpine Forest’s eastern edge beside Lordamere Lake. Several aggressive Vile Fin murloc settlements line the shallows and threaten travelers on the lake road. Feral worgen roam the deep woods behind the shore.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_shining-strand-715f4cd4c4d81703d1f5/1-0000.mp3", duration = 28.1338776, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {
  hash = "532e7c",
  fullHash = "532e7c",
  text = "Shrine of the Dormant Flame. At the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, Horde shaman seek communion with fire atop Durotar’s highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials. Telf Joolam keeps the secluded sanctuary, where initiates climb to prove their spiritual mastery. A narrow trail winds up from the Southfury River, at the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed. The summit rises above Durotar’s red cliffs, with a commanding view and a precipice where one misstep means certain death. Telf Joolam, a solitary hermit, oversees the sacred rites here. Aspiring orc and troll shaman come for the ritual Call of Fire. At the shrine’s brazier, they use the ember of a defeated elemental to kindle the sleeping coals and prove they can commune with fire and respect its destructive spirits.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_shrine-of-the-dormant-flame-67aee4e99e1c141bb6b4/1-0000.mp3", duration = 44.7477551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:shrine-of-the-fallen-warrior"] = {
  hash = "4cd835",
  fullHash = "d12b36",
  text = "Shrine of the Fallen Warrior. At the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior, Koiter watches over an orc laid to rest on a ridge west of the Crossroads. A stone plinth marked 'MK' keeps the warrior's memory beneath the Barrens sky. High on the hills northwest of the Crossroads, the shrine offers a quiet place amid the Barrens' dust and peril. Find the ridge southwest of the summit and follow its winding path to a gentle mound. A carved stone monument rests at the top, its plinth marked with the initials 'MK'.\n\nAn armored orc warrior lies before it, watched day and night by Koiter, a Spirit Healer. No battle horns sound here. The shrine honors a champion who walked Kalimdor's lands. The shrine honors a departed champion of the Horde. The warrior's soul lingers in the spirits' care, beneath the watch of Koiter.\n\nThe monument also remembers Michel Koiter, an illustrator who died while the world was being made. The resting warrior was modeled on Koiter's own early character, Twincruiser, and his memory remains beneath Kalimdor's open skies.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_shrine-of-the-fallen-warrior-b33800b986dae250d784/1-0000.mp3", duration = 65.0187755, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:skittering-dark"] = {
  hash = "6d9cb9",
  fullHash = "6d9cb9",
  text = "Skittering Dark. Giant spiders now hunt through Skittering Dark and the nearby woods in western Silverpine. The abandoned mine and its approaches are dangerous to beasts and travelers alike. East of North Tide's Run, Skittering Dark lies where the western coast meets the hills. The mine once worked, but now cobwebs choke its shafts and giant spiders nest through the hollow. Krethis haunts the shadowed woods outside. The spiders hunt anything that strays too close.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_skittering-dark-478217ed5ce0dc52430b/1-0000.mp3", duration = 27.3763265, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:skull-rock"] = {
  hash = "c7bf72",
  fullHash = "c7bf72",
  text = "Skull Rock. Burning Blade cultists gather at Skull Rock, hidden in Durotar's eastern coastal cliffs. Their cavern lies east of Orgrimmar, where they plot against Thrall's Horde. Burning Blade cultists gather in Skull Rock, a perilous stronghold beneath northeastern Durotar's crags. Dark cultists, fel-worshipping orcs, and summoners meet in its winding tunnels to practice demonic arts and plot against the young Horde. The warlock Gazz'uz leads the cell. Its work threatens Orgrimmar's nearby gates and travelers along the eastern shore.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_skull-rock-787e6b198ef579074aba/1-0000.mp3", duration = 31.0595918, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:sludge-fen"] = {
  hash = "dd925f",
  fullHash = "dd925f",
  text = "Sludge Fen. In northeastern the Barrens, Sludge Fen's clear pool has become an oily industrial field run by the Venture Company. Supervisor Lugwizzle oversees the drilling, while rivals in Ratchet seek to sabotage the operation. Sludge Fen once held a clear pool fed by natural springs in the arid Barrens. The Venture Company built oil-drilling platforms and machinery over the basin, turning the wetland into a reservoir of sludge and industrial waste. Supervisor Lugwizzle oversees goblin drillers, engineers, and overseers as they pump crude oil around the clock. Runoff and toxic byproducts coat the water, choking the native aquatic life beneath the grease.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_sludge-fen-88f95a2c46764d7cf447/1-0000.mp3", duration = 37.8514286, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:solliden-farmstead"] = {
  hash = "d466c1",
  fullHash = "1eaf35",
  text = "Solliden Farmstead. In western Tirisfal Glades, Solliden Farmstead’s human farmers still tend pumpkins north of Deathknell. Native Lordaeronians who survived the Plague of Undeath are rare in northern Lordaeron, and they cling fiercely to their soil beneath the Scarlet Crusade’s shadow. Solliden Farmstead’s fields still yield healthy crops, though much of Lordaeron lies in ruin and rot. The surviving human farmers are traumatized and keep to themselves. Scarlet Crusade patrols watch them from a nearby tower. They defend their home fiercely, striking at outsiders who come near, Horde or Alliance alike. Forsaken rising from Deathknell see Solliden Farmstead as both threat and resource. The Royal Apothecary Society wants its pristine pumpkins for testing and brewing the New Plague. So Forsaken officers such as Deathguard Simmer send fledgling recruits to raid the fields and steal pumpkins for Apothecary Johaan in Brill. They are also sent to teach the living a lesson.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_solliden-farmstead-cd975771e3cd1fcbe02d/1-0000.mp3", duration = 58.0702041, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:south-tide-s-run"] = {
  hash = "ea64b0",
  fullHash = "ea64b0",
  text = "South Tide's Run. Along Silverpine Forest's southwestern edge, South Tide's Run meets the cold Great Sea. Its damp shore borders the forested interior and lies south of North Tide's Run. The Great Sea washes Silverpine Forest's southwestern shore. Inland, roads run east toward the Greymane Wall beneath the forest's cover. Along this open coast, the western tides meet a bleak stretch, largely untouched by inland settlements.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_south-tide-s-run-e7c685ac0e3ef2c6d658/1-0000.mp3", duration = 27.6636735, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:southern-gold-road"] = {
  hash = "003aee",
  fullHash = "eb1e2a",
  text = "Southern Gold Road. Caravans and travelers crowd the Southern Gold Road as it runs through the Barrens toward the Great Lift. Trade links the central plains with distant reaches of Kalimdor. At the stone bridge between the northern and southern Barrens, the Southern Gold Road turns south toward the Great Lift and Thousand Needles. Like the northern stretch, simply called the Gold Road, it takes its name from the lucrative merchant caravans that travel its length. Quilboar tribes and prowling predators harass those who use it, yet the road remains one of the continent’s busiest long-distance routes. Goods pass along it between remote outposts and ports. Horde couriers and patrols share the Southern Gold Road with merchants and explorers bound for distant lands. Travelers journey between Gadgetzan in the southern deserts of Tanaris, Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore, and Nighthaven, among the sacred groves of Moonglade. For those crossing Kalimdor’s interior on foot, surviving the journey down this sun-baked road is a grueling rite of passage.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_southern-gold-road-788c18fc6c106d78e9fd/1-0000.mp3", duration = 59.8465306, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:spirit-rise"] = {
  hash = "df15d2",
  fullHash = "63fd9f",
  text = "Spirit Rise. On Thunder Bluff’s northwest mesa, Spirit Rise gathers shaman and seekers. The Skychaser tribe guides them above the Pools of Vision, where seers peer into spirit-touched waters. Spirit Rise crowns Thunder Bluff above the plains of Mulgore. Here, shaman seek communion with the elements and ancestor spirits. Rope bridges link the rise to the central mesa.\n\nThe Hall of Spirits and the Spiritual Healing pavilion draw young and veteran shaman alike. They come to deepen their bond with earth, air, fire, and water. The Skychaser tribe keeps a strong presence here and guides seekers in ancient traditions. Below the open-air totem shrines and huts, an entrance leads into the mesa. There, the steamy Pools of Vision fill a sacred cavern. Seers peer into waters touched by the spirits.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_spirit-rise-7f5e8a7cc14ad6c4b583/1-0000.mp3", duration = 50.5991837, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:spirit-rock"] = {
  hash = "66602d",
  fullHash = "66602d",
  text = "Spirit Rock. Above the Valley of Trials in Durotar, Spirit Rock draws Horde initiates to commune with the elements. A winding trail called the Hidden Path leads to this sacred crag. Spirit Rock overlooks the red canyon where young Horde warriors and scouts train. The Hidden Path winds up the rocky ridgeline to this quiet altar. Aspiring shaman climb to the outcrop and drink sapta, a traditional brew that opens their senses beyond the physical world. They listen for the earth's rumblings and whispers.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_spirit-rock-34e1834257fc3ae0e34f/1-0000.mp3", duration = 27.9510204, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:stagnant-oasis"] = {
  hash = "efb088",
  fullHash = "6aa7df",
  text = "Stagnant Oasis. Kolkar centaur guard the Stagnant Oasis in the dry heart of the Barrens. Its waters lie between the Gold Road and Merchant Coast, drawing wildlife to its banks. East of the Gold Road, inland from the Merchant Coast, the Stagnant Oasis breaks up the dusty scrub of the Barrens. Dense foliage grows around the pool, where aggressive snapjaw turtles prowl. Weakened kodos often stray here from the great herds of the Field of Giants. Kolkar centaur keep camps along the banks and fiercely guard the water from anyone entering their territory. Strange life stirs in the pool, though its waters look still. Deviate Fish swim among other unusual creatures. Scholars and shamans watch the Barrens oases closely, studying the strange forces that affect local springheads and the wildlife that drinks from them.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_stagnant-oasis-75eeda4fbdadf177bf58/1-0000.mp3", duration = 48.2481633, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:stillwater-pond"] = {
  hash = "49b2dd",
  fullHash = "5b1012",
  text = "Stillwater Pond. Just west of Brill, Stillwater Pond lies gray and lifeless, a lost refuge for Lordaeron's children. Families from nearby hamlets once picnicked on Stillwater Pond's grassy banks. Before the Third War and the Plague of Undeath, its shallows let children too young to brave Brightwater Lake learn to swim. Now the water is gray and lifeless. The living have vanished, leaving skeletal fish below and wandering undead in the woods around it. Stillwater Pond is quieter than Tirisfal's besieged roads and contested farms, yet danger lingers along its shore. Blighted beasts drink from the murky water, including Bayne, a ferocious darkhound that stalks the banks. Travelers crossing the western meadows toward Brill must watch for predatory beasts and aimless zombies by the water's edge.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_stillwater-pond-7bb05c132924cd95418c/1-0000.mp3", duration = 47.1771429, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:stonebull-lake"] = {
  hash = "9ef5d6",
  fullHash = "9ef5d6",
  text = "Stonebull Lake. At Stonebull Lake, tauren draw fresh water and fish from the heart of Mulgore. Stonebull Lake curves around Bloodhoof Village on three sides, at the heart of central Mulgore. A wooden bridge spans its narrowest stretch. The main dirt road crosses there, linking the village with Thunder Bluff on the great mesa to the north. Native fish fill the calm water. Hunters rest on the banks, travelers pause, and apprentice fishers learn their trade beneath the open sky.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_stonebull-lake-fda90a547b4067c8eefb/1-0000.mp3", duration = 28.8130612, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:the-den"] = {
  hash = "0e9c7b",
  fullHash = "587bad",
  text = "The Den. In southwestern Durotar, young orcs and trolls gather at the sheltered Den in the heart of the Valley of Trials. It is their main base, where they train in arms and magic before setting out into the wider world. The Den is an austere proving ground, carved into the red canyon walls of the Valley of Trials. Inside its shadowed halls, novice fighters, spellcasters, and hunters answer to veterans such as Gornek and Zureetha Fargaze. They receive their first combat lessons, supplies, and rites of passage, preparing for Durotar's harshness and the struggles facing the new Horde. The Den houses class trainers and merchants who provide provisions. From this field outpost, overseers send recruits to cull local beasts and aggressive quilboars. They keep a strict watch over the valley.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_the-den-9b69e536e8d384a55ad8/1-0000.mp3", duration = 46.7069388, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:thorn-hill"] = {
  hash = "8dcb29",
  fullHash = "8dcb29",
  text = "Thorn Hill. Razormane warbands strike Horde supply lines from Thorn Hill, east of the Crossroads. The fortified quilboar camp holds the high ridges between Durotar and the Barrens interior. Thorn Hill overlooks the roads between Durotar and the Crossroads. The Razormane gather here with hunters, trained wolves, and geomancers who shape the earth. Elder Mystic Razorsnout guides the quilboar as their attacks on Horde supply caravans grow bolder. The camp sits close to vital routes, making it one of the Crossroads guards' most immediate threats in the central savanna.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_thorn-hill-2caf198a7571079faa4e/1-0000.mp3", duration = 33.7763265, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:thunder-ridge"] = {
  hash = "395791",
  fullHash = "395791",
  text = "Thunder Ridge. Thunder Ridge lies southwest of Orgrimmar, where thunder lizards roam a stripped canyon. Along the Southfury River in western Durotar, the former grove was ruined by human logging and dark sorcery. Agitated beasts and lingering cultists threaten nearby settlements. Thunder Ridge was once a green haven in arid Durotar, shaded by ancient trees. Shortly after the Third War, humans from Kul Tiras began felling its timber. The thunder lizards grew wild as their home was cut away. Then the Burning Blade used fel sorcery to destroy what remained of the canopy. Now the gorge lies barren and exposed, with angry, lightning-spewing beasts roaming through it.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_thunder-ridge-8124312053dbfac170e9/1-0000.mp3", duration = 42.24, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:thunderhorn-water-well"] = {
  hash = "1abe31",
  fullHash = "1abe31",
  text = "Thunderhorn Water Well. At Thunderhorn Water Well, tauren and their herds draw water in central Mulgore. The well lies along the path from Bloodhoof Village to Thunder Bluff, where the valley’s wells sustain life across the grasslands. The tauren must keep them clean and defended. Thunderhorn Water Well draws water from aquifers beneath central Mulgore. Nomadic tauren and settled villages alike rely on communal wells for water and sustenance. Across the plains, water is precious, and whoever controls the wells controls the land.\n\nThe Venture Company has repeatedly sought these water sources for industrial use. Their efforts threaten the balance the tribes work to preserve.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_thunderhorn-water-well-294fcd3ba33d73b8aa84/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.6277551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:tidus-stair"] = {
  hash = "3bd9e0",
  fullHash = "3bd9e0",
  text = "Tidus Stair. At Tidus Stair, two tauren shamans seek insight from the coastal water spirits. Broad stone terraces rise above the Merchant Coast southeast of Ratchet, sheltered beside the Great Sea. Waves crash below the weathered stone terraces of Tidus Stair, cut into the coastal bluffs southeast of Ratchet. The Barrens around you are arid and dusty, and skirmishes trouble the region, but this stretch above the Merchant Coast is quiet. A modest hut stands on the terraces, home to the tauren Islen Waterseer and Mahren Skyseer. Far from the goblin trade docks, they spend their days fishing, watching the horizon, and seeking insight from the coastal water spirits.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_tidus-stair-63ad4e5a1367f3480a5e/1-0000.mp3", duration = 41.3779592, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:tiragarde-keep"] = {
  hash = "99f7e6",
  fullHash = "9cccf3",
  text = "Tiragarde Keep. Kul Tiran marines still hold Tiragarde Keep on Durotar's Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill. Built during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion, the ruined stronghold remains garrisoned under Lieutenant Benedict, a hostile thorn in the Horde's own territory. Tiragarde Keep gave Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet a beachhead on Durotar's red shores. He built it during his campaign to destroy Thrall's newly founded realm. The Horde eventually broke the siege and killed Proudmoore at Theramore Isle, but the keep was never fully abandoned. Resupply forces under Lieutenant Benedict reclaimed its shattered stone walls. They follow the late Admiral's standing orders to wage unyielding war against the orcs and reject the peace Lady Jaina Proudmoore forged. White battlements rise above Durotar's crimson cliffs, and Kul Tiran sailors and marines patrol them. The garrison raids supply lines near Razor Hill. For the Horde, the keep remains an ongoing security crisis and a live proving ground: orc and troll commanders send young warriors to assault the fortress and cut down Benedict's soldiers. They seek to contain the garrison before the humans can push farther inland.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_tiragarde-keep-fd0e38601dcf245813c7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 69.5902041, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:tor-kren-farm"] = {
  hash = "95c1bf",
  fullHash = "d4bcc7",
  text = "Tor'kren Farm. At Tor'kren Farm in northwestern Durotar, Misha Tor'kren waits anxiously for news of her son Kron. He has not returned from a hunting trip. Tor'kren Farm struggles to raise pigs in Durotar's dry red dirt. The homestead lies southeast of Thunder Ridge, near the Southfury River. Feed and water are scarce, and the farm is isolated beneath nearby bluffs. Its yields are meager. Kron went west several days ago to hunt crocolisks along the Southfury River. Misha Tor'kren warned him about the vicious predators, but he left in anger. Now she asks passing adventurers to search for him or bring back a sign of his fate. She fears the worst, but cannot begin mourning without knowing what happened.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_tor-kren-farm-bfd302c5e9c5121702e7/1-0000.mp3", duration = 43.1281633, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:trade-quarter"] = {
  hash = "b0b4d5",
  fullHash = "b0b4d5",
  text = "Trade Quarter. Trade Quarter draws the Undercity’s commerce and civic life beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron. Its bank, auction house, and other services serve the Forsaken capital, while corridors link it to the surrounding districts. You step from the lifts beneath the Ruins of Lordaeron into the Trade Quarter’s broad, circular halls. Canals of noxious runoff circle the central platform, crossed by bridges. The city’s coffers and bank rest there, while vendors, guild registrars, and auctioneers work along the terraces. At the inn, wooden caskets replace soft beds. Stone archways lead into the other districts, drawing the Undercity’s business through its center.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_trade-quarter-bdd84257e3a3df039dc0/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.444898, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:valgan-s-field"] = {
  hash = "bbb598",
  fullHash = "bbb598",
  text = "Valgan's Field. Worgen roam Valgan's Field above Lordamere Lake in northern Silverpine Forest. Arugal unleashed the Moonrage pack, and the Forsaken now search the ruined farm for his abandoned research. West of the Shining Strand and north of the nearby river, Valgan's Field overlooks Lordamere Lake. The wheat farm once prospered, until the Scourge swept through Lordaeron and forced Valgan to flee or die. Left untended, its buildings fell to feral Moonrage worgen prowling down from Shadowfang Keep. Before the Third War, Arugal spent time here and left remnants of his arcane research. Now the Forsaken seek them.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_valgan-s-field-0f8437e8621b19dcc8c1/1-0000.mp3", duration = 37.6163265, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:valley-of-honor"] = {
  hash = "5b627d",
  fullHash = "747ac4",
  text = "Valley of Honor. In the Valley of Honor, Orgrimmar's warriors and hunters prepare for battle. Its barracks, guilds, and battlemasters serve the Horde's forces across Azeroth, while forges and training grounds keep its fighters ready. The Valley of Honor holds Orgrimmar's military quarter behind high canyon ridges. Practice weapons clash, and blacksmiths' anvils ring through the day. The Hall of the Brave draws seasoned warriors and battlemasters who coordinate campaigns in places such as Alterac Valley and Warsong Gulch. Training grounds for beastmasters and hunters flank the hall. Across the valley, the Horde equips, drills, and sends out its frontline defenders. The valley supplies arms and offers a place to rest between duties. The Burning Anvil and Red Canyon Mining provide armor and raw iron, while engineers work nearby in Nogg's Machine Shop. Grunts and visiting adventurers can fish in a quiet pool, taking a brief pause from the dust of the Valley of Strength.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_valley-of-honor-c10ba1a43575d3c4c5fc/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.04, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:valley-of-spirits"] = {
  hash = "ecc975",
  fullHash = "1f464a",
  text = "Valley of Spirits. Darkspear trolls make their home in the Valley of Spirits, west of Orgrimmar's main thoroughfares. Thatched lodges, tiki poles, and pools mark their place among the city's red stone and iron. The Valley of Spirits branches west from the Valley of Strength, a quiet enclave for the Darkspear trolls. The tribe settled in Durotar alongside Thrall's orcs, and made this pocket among the crags their gathering place in the city. Trollish craftspeople, spiritualists, and practitioners gather around wooden bridges and winding waters, practicing their arts away from the dry heat of Orgrimmar's main thoroughfares. The valley's lodges and pools draw those who practice magic and wild crafts. Witch doctors, herbalists, and spellcasters gather at the Spirit Lodge and Darkbriar Lodge. At the back, the Talon Gate opens toward the Barrens' open plains, giving wanderers, hunters, and travelers a quick passage beyond the canyon walls.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_valley-of-spirits-2954965123b189e39c8f/1-0000.mp3", duration = 55.3534694, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:valley-of-strength"] = {
  hash = "9cdf88",
  fullHash = "11e14d",
  text = "Valley of Strength. Trade and daily business fill Orgrimmar's Valley of Strength. The bank, central auction house, and Broken Tusk inn draw travelers through the Horde capital. Beyond Orgrimmar's timber gates, the Valley of Strength opens among Durotar's red canyon walls. Adventurers, merchants, and warriors from allied nations fill the Horde's front square. At the Broken Tusk inn, some trade war stories over flagons. Others turn to business at the central bank and auction house. The orcs fought for strength and unity in their new homeland, and both shape the city's heart. The Valley of Strength is Orgrimmar's foremost marketplace. Soran's Leather and Steel Armory sells armor, while vendors stock provisions for long treks across the Barrens. Grunts watch every corner. They guide newcomers and keep order among the diverse peoples who have taken refuge beneath Thrall's banner.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_valley-of-strength-593a3cfd09975ebb6dff/1-0000.mp3", duration = 54.2563265, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:venomweb-vale"] = {
  hash = "c7e434",
  fullHash = "c7e434",
  text = "Venomweb Vale. South of the Scarlet Monastery, Venomweb Vale lies under a swarm of venomous spiders. Once, hunters tracked deer and rabbits through its woodland. Venomweb Vale has lost its peaceful hunting ground to rot and gloom. Before the plague consumed Lordaeron, hunters followed deer and rabbits through its grass and trees. Now giant venomous spiders swarm through the trees and hollows, led by the monstrous Sri'skulk.\n\nTo the north, the Scarlet Crusade holds the neighboring territory. Darkhounds prowl near the fortified Scarlet Encampment, where Lieutenant Sanders commands.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_venomweb-vale-eb4cfb65615150bba32d/1-0000.mp3", duration = 36.7281633, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:venture-co-mine"] = {
  hash = "eaa3da",
  fullHash = "eaa3da",
  text = "Venture Co. Mine. In Mulgore’s eastern cliffs, Venture Co. Mine scars land the tauren hold sacred. The goblin company digs without permission, disturbing the plains’ natural balance. The Venture Company tunnels through Mulgore’s eastern mountain wall, though the tauren refused it mining rights. Supervisor Fizsprocket directs the work. Three entrances lead inside: a ground tunnel guarded by hired muscle, a cliffside overlook, and an upper passage to a small lumber camp. Machines, smoke, and slag heaps scar land the tauren hold sacred.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_venture-co-mine-54bd47e460c875207169/1-0000.mp3", duration = 31.8693878, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:war-quarter"] = {
  hash = "87fe29",
  fullHash = "6cc0c6",
  text = "War Quarter. In the War Quarter, Lordaeron's Forsaken hone weapons and shadow magic for their fledgling kingdom. Training halls, weapon masters, and heavy industry fill the Undercity's northwest. Rank-and-file guards and elite champions drill beneath the War Quarter's gloomy stone arches. There, ruthless iron warfare meets the chilling rites of shadow. The Altar of Darkness stands at its heart. Warrior and priest guilds make the War Quarter the heart of Undercity's wartime production. Blacksmiths and smelters ring the stone with their labor as weapon masters prepare blades and armor. Iron forged deep underground arms the forces defending Lordaeron's ruins from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_war-quarter-f40b63f07c76f56b0063/1-0000.mp3", duration = 44.4081633, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:whispering-forest"] = {
  hash = "20ef26",
  fullHash = "20ef26",
  text = "Whispering Forest. Behind Deathknell, the Whispering Forest lies quiet beneath western Tirisfal’s cliffs. Its lake, giant mushroom ring, and uncanny wildlife break the stillness, while corruption stirs beneath the soil. Beyond Northface Rock and Bandarion Keep, the Whispering Forest feels far from plague-touched Tirisfal. Afflicted deer and roaming predators share its woods with a tranquil lake. Nearby, giant mushrooms form a ring beneath a hovering cloud of mist, glowing with uncanny energy. The ghostly Knight of Mourning wanders among them, bound by oath. Natural magic lingers here in land scarred by the Scourge.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_whispering-forest-d254a0cb67aa78c9b9b1/1-0000.mp3", duration = 39.9934694, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:whispering-shore"] = {
  hash = "03a14a",
  fullHash = "a3a2f1",
  text = "Whispering Shore. Along Tirisfal Glades' western coast, the Whispering Shore lies north of Solliden Farmstead. Hostile murlocs claim its waters. Before the Third War, Lordaeron's fishermen came to the Whispering Shore for calm water and plentiful catches. Now the Great Sea breaks against an empty coast. Its waters are cold and dark, and travelers descending from the hills risk ambush by murlocs along the shore. Hostile murlocs claim the beach and attack anyone who approaches the surf. Their chieftain, Muad, leads them as they guard the shallows and tidal flats. Nearby roads and Solliden Farmstead are under threat.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_whispering-shore-417a4f74dec7f5a88886/1-0000.mp3", duration = 36.4669388, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:wildmane-water-well"] = {
  hash = "9c40a9",
  fullHash = "9c40a9",
  text = "Wildmane Water Well. Wildmane Water Well lies under threat as poisoned water endangers Mulgore’s northern plains and the herds that depend on it. Sacred wells sustain the tauren and their wandering kodo herds across Mulgore. Wildmane Water Well lies at the northern edge of the plains, beyond Thunder Bluff’s shadow. Venture Company goblins have poisoned its water to control the regional supply. A totem crafted by the tauren is needed to cleanse the well and make its water pure again.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_wildmane-water-well-359ae09b2c73d9f15969/1-0000.mp3", duration = 27.637551, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:windfury-ridge"] = {
  hash = "655361",
  fullHash = "655361",
  text = "Windfury Ridge. Windfury Ridge rises above Mulgore’s pastures, where harpies nest among wolves and cougars. Its slopes endanger travelers, and tauren hunters seek the harpies’ feathers. Windfury Ridge rises above Mulgore’s plains, its crags home to Windfury harpies. They swoop at wanderers who stray too close. Prairie wolves and mountain cougars prowl the rocky slopes, making this edge of the tauren heartland dangerous. Tauren warriors hunt the harpies for their iridescent feathers, sought in Thunder Bluff for ceremonial garments worn at feasts and weddings.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_windfury-ridge-1a29b131f26b3d70546d/1-0000.mp3", duration = 33.7763265, start = 0},
  },
}
P.transport["subzone:winterhoof-water-well"] = {
  hash = "72844f",
  fullHash = "72844f",
  text = "Winterhoof Water Well. Winterhoof Water Well faces a threat to Mulgore’s water supply from the Venture Company. South of Bloodhoof Village, it stands at the edge of the Rolling Plains, where tauren tribes and roaming herds depend on its fresh water. Deep wells sustain Mulgore’s herds and tauren encampments. Winterhoof Water Well draws from aquifers beneath the Rolling Plains and takes its name from one of the plains’ respected tribes. Now the Venture Company has targeted this vital source. The goblin cartel seeks control of the surrounding territory and has tried to poison the water.",
  ["1"] = {
    {file = "Audio/Transport/full_subzone_winterhoof-water-well-fe255bf5532170c8dfe2/1-0000.mp3", duration = 32.1828571, start = 0},
  },
}
